[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1]
Pass On

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1_desc]
The second day after “Jahr Null”, a major event occurred also among the Kirins: Rain Shine announced to the Kirins that she would abdicate and pass on the leadership of the Kirins to the most outstanding Kirin, Autumn Blaze.
Although Rain Shine’s abdication marked an important change, the Kirins were already prepared. For several months, Rain Shine had begun to gradually reduce her public activities and hand over more affairs to Autumn Blaze. Autumn Blaze also demonstrated her ability during this time, giving the Kirins more confidence in her leadership ability - or rather, the Kirins had already regarded this greatest contributor to the end of the Kirin silence as the future leader at the very beginning.
Rain Shine said, “The occurrence of ‘Jahr Null’ was indeed unexpected to me, but my abdication is not directly related to ‘Jahr Null’. After all, the Kirinthal continent is too far away to be affected much: ‘I am a pacifist, but I am also a realist. I know that the world situation is changing now, and the Kirin country has become more open in recent years. I believe that in such a turbulent and challenging era, the energetic leader Autumn Blaze, compared to me who only pursues stability, can better lead the Kirin country to the future and seize opportunities.”
On the other hand, Rain Shine also said that since her voice had recovered, she had always wanted to return to the entertainment industry.
“I was once a leader, but since then I want to be a singer again.” Rain Shine said.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1_o0]
Rejoice, rejoice

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2]
Where Flowers Bloom

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2_desc]
“Here you are, Autumn Blaze.” Rain Shine stood on the open balcony of the garden, turning around to face Autumn Blaze who had just walked in.
Autumn Blaze walked to Rain Shine’s side and looked up at her. Before Autumn Blaze could say anything, Rain Shine spoke again, “Starting tomorrow, this place will be yours. But before that, I have one more question for you.”
This seemed to be an exam question prepared by the retiring leader for the successor Autumn Blaze. Autumn Blaze respectfully nodded, indicating Rain Shine to continue.

“If one day, the Niriks appear again in this land, what will you do?”
Autumn Blaze immediately answered, “Leader, I believe that my most important task after taking over is to prevent such things from happening again.”
“No, let’s say it has already happened, with no chance of redemption. For the survival of the Kirins, you will have to face your fellows with arms. What will you do then?” Rain Shine immediately rejected Autumn Blaze’s answer.
After a long silence, Autumn Blaze hesitated and answered, “I will do my best to mediate the conflict and avoid unnecessary casualties. But if it is inevitable, I will let the Kirins take up arms. The Kirins will survive, even if it means that some of us, or even I myself, become Niriks or die on the battlefield, even if it means facing my former fellows and dear friends with arms, I will choose to do so.”

After listening, Rain Shine immediately closed her eyes, turned her head away, looking very disappointed and heartbroken. Autumn Blaze looked at Rain Shine’s back and expression, and asked carefully, “So, Leader, do you think I made the wrong choice? What kind of choice do you want me to make?”
Does the Leader want us to lay down our weapons and surrender? Or be slaughtered by those crazy Niriks? Autumn Blaze was puzzled, but did not say it out loud.
Rain Shine just shook her head, “No, this question has no answer. I just wanted to hear your thoughts.” Seeing Autumn Blaze’s puzzled and somewhat worried expression, Rain Shine continued:
“Autumn Blaze, you have made your choice, and there is no turning back. After taking over, please seriously prepare for the upcoming war.”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2_o0]
“What?”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3]
Climate Risk Assessment

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3_desc]
Some meteorological observers who returned from studying abroad in Equestria, together with professional meteorologists we invited from Ponyville, have analyzed the data from several observation stations near the Southern Peaks of Peril and Kirin Isles with us. We have come to the following conclusion:
In the past year, the activity of the Windigos has indeed increased worldwide. However, when cross-referencing the data from the Kirin commune local areas near the southern Windigo territory with the global data, we did not observe any significant differences.
This means that the increased activity of the Windigos has not brought any additional cooling, snowfall, or any climate risks to the Kirin tribes. In contrast, the data shows that areas such as Seaquestria and Kluge Town have more severe cooling trends, and the relevant parties need to be more vigilant.
In conclusion, the report believes that the Kirin are currently not threatened by climate risks, but in the face of a global climate change, we still need to work together with other countries to maintain our efforts.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4]
Foal Mania

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_desc]
In the initial opening to the outside world, we found that our specialty flower “Foal’s Breath” is the most popular in the international market among all exported goods. This flower, which emits a faint fragrance, also has the effect of refreshing the mind, allowing the user to think quickly and speak fluently.
Different from the high-end decorative flowers recognized by the outside world, “Foal’s Breath” is an important strategic material for the Kirin —— the only antidote to the “Silence”. For a long time, due to the large quantity of “Foal’s Breath” is needed to lift the “Silence”, the government strictly limited its export to prioritize domestic supply, which further raised the price of “Foal’s Breath”.
Now that the “Silence” has been successfully lifted nationwide, “Foal’s Breath” is no longer our necessity, and there are countless plantations across the country growing this flower. Perhaps it is time to lift this restriction and allow more farmers who grow “Foal’s Breath” to improve their lives.
However, experts warn that fully opening the export of “Foal’s Breath” may lead to a drop in its price and a decrease in planting profits. We may need to consider this more carefully.
Apart from the economy, a more important concern is: the centaurs have not been very interested in us before. In their stereotyped impression, the Kirin commune is nothing more than an uncivilized tribe in the jungle. That’s why we were lucky to escape most of the centaur’s exploitation after the Ultimate Battle. But when “Foal’s Breath” becomes a hot trend among the upper-class of the centaurs, will we attract the attention of Tirek?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o0]
Fully Allow Free Export

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o1]
Relax Export Control

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o2]
Maintain Status Quo

[en.C18_DRAW_ATTENTION_1_TOOLITP]
We §Ymay§! attract the attention of §R[C22.GetName]§!.

[en.C18_DRAW_ATTENTION_2_TOOLITP]
We §Ymay very likely§! attract the attention of §R[C22.GetName]§!.

[en.C18_LESS_ATTENTION_1_TOOLTIP]
We will be less likely to be noticed by §R[C22.GetName]§!.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8]
Unexpected Guest

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8_desc]
The Applejack Harbour market is the most lively place in the Kirin community, even more so than the capital Peaks of Peril. Here you can see all kinds of Kirins, ponies, griffons, metamorphosed changelings, and even some imperial officials who come to sell stolen goods.
Merchant ships come and go, each one representing countless wealth and opportunities. Compared to the shouting and yelling, here you are more likely to hear the sound of coins pouring out of bags, development bonds being slapped on wooden tables, goods sliding off wooden ships, bosses hooves clapping, shoulders patting, or pipes being lit. Such a transaction, for those solitary Kirins in the Kirin Forest, may be a lifetime of wealth.

Hidden among the giant cargo ships, a small wooden boat quietly docked. Several cloaked ponies, whose faces were completely covered, walked down from the ship and automatically lined up in two rows, following their leader - a cloaked pony with a cane, walking towards the market further away from the dock. Along the way, they stopped from time to time to watch the bosses leaning on the goods with their pipes, talking business with the local Kirins. However, they seemed more interested in the young Kirin nomads who were carrying the goods with their glowing horns. The cloaked team finally stopped in front of a small shop in the market, with a sign that read “Kirin Movers”.
The leader stood at the door and knocked twice with his cane. Hearing the sound, a Kirin shopkeeper quickly opened the door and greeted them. Seeing the cloaked ponies behind him, her business eyes immediately lit up: “Oh! Such a big lineup! Just one glance, and I know you are a big boss from out of town! You have a lot of goods to move, right? The magic of the young Kirins in our shop is top-notch in the Kirin commune. The goods of several ships can be moved in a few hours! Since you are a big boss, we seek to form a long-term partnership with you, and I will give you a huge discount! What do you think? We have branches all over the country, so even if you go to Fluttershy Harbour or Peaks of Peril, we can provide you with the best service!”

From the deep, invisible darkness under the cloak, the old and heavy voice of the leader finally sounded: “Magic? That’s exactly what I expected.” The leader slowly took off the hood of the cloak —
It was a centaur.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8_o0]
Alert!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9]
Alert

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9_desc]
After the shopkeeper frantically rang the bell to report the case, the market patrol quickly arrived at the front of the “Kirin Movers” shop and surrounded the cloaked centaur team. They seemed to have no signs of resistance, just standing quietly without saying a word.
The appearance of centaurs quickly disturbed the market, and the entire port dock was evacuated. Kirin military leader Burnt Umber quickly arrived at the scene. After confirming that the centaurs seemed to have no hostility, Burnt Umber walked up and began to talk to the leader.
“Though it’s not the first time we’ve seen centaurs at the port, it might be your first time, so let me explain. We can never let Tirek be interested in this port, so after the centaurs come here, they have only three choices: first, to live forever in the Kirin commune and never go back. Second, we will knock you out and throw you into the jungle to fend for yourself, but rest assured, the herbs will only make the target lose memory and are not poisonous. Third, in the worst case, we will be forced to —”
The leader knocked on the ground again with his cane, interrupting Burnt Umber. “It seems you don’t know me. So, to put it simply, just as you are on guard against Tirek, Tirek is also my enemy. I am here to seek cooperation.”
Burnt Umber obviously did not expect this situation. The previous centaurs were either ignorant nobles who accidentally broke in, or centaur colonizers. The former generally received one of the first two options, while the latter generally received the third option. Just as Burnt Umber was about to ask in detail, the leader preempted him and said, “I won’t answer your questions. Call your leader over. I can only discuss such important matters with your highest leader.”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9_o0]
Emm... okay?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10]
Suspicious Cooperation

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10_desc]
The next day, as soon as Sendak stepped into Autumn Blaze’s treehouse, Autumn Blaze immediately began her endless chatter: “Sendak, right? Tirek’s teacher, the ambitious centaur, the unicorn magic enthusiast. Seeing your background, it’s hard for me to believe in the saying ‘the enemy of my enemy is my friend’. But there’s nothing serious on your background, hmm... except that you once kidnapped a unicorn. Anyway, if you are not so fixated on the so-called ‘cooperation’ matter, why not let us arrange some good accommodations for you and your guys? Oh by the way, our musical ‘The Phantom of the Opera’ is recently re-released, of course, I mean, if you cloaked guys are interested in some company team-bonding.”
Sendak smiled slightly: “You are really a leader who knows how to talk, how should I address you? If you have really done enough background checks, you should know that I am the kind of centaur who prefers to get straight to the point. I know you have been on guard against Tirek, not daring to fully open up for fear of attracting his attention, so if we get rid of Tirek together, you get complete freedom, and I get the magic I want, isn’t this a win-win situation?”
Autumn Blaze continued her lengthy speech: “Oh, wow! You want to take down Tirek? I mean, we have thought about it, but, you know, Tirek is a big guy, and we don’t want to mess with him. You don’t look very strong, oh sorry, I mean you look a bit old, oh sorry, I mean you don’t look like a guy who can take down Tirek. But if you can really help us deal with Tirek, we will of course be very grateful! However, you should know that we are not the kind of species that easily believes in — oh, right, almost forgot, Autumn Blaze, you can call me Autumn Blaze.”
Sendak took out a hastily written document: “I already have a way, but if I explain it to you here, I’m afraid I will have to listen to you talk about the entire script of ‘The Phantom of the Opera’ all day. Read the document yourself, make up your mind and contact me, our port is on the small island opposite Applejack Harbour.” With that, Sendak turned and left the treehouse.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10_o0]
Prevent spoilers, smart

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11]
Sendak’s Plan

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_desc]
Before finding the unicorn, Sendak and his church had secretly contacted forces in various places in Equestria: Tirek’s brother Scorpan, griffons, scientists in Las Pegasus, even Discord and Zecora. However, the results were very disappointing. The current giant Tirek, like a mountain, is almost invincible, with no weaknesses.
As a result, there is only one way to deal with Tirek: brute force. Gather an enormous amount of magic, forcibly break through Tirek’s magic shield in an instant to knock him down. Sendak’s church has made careful calculations and found that the minimum magic level required for this process, even though it is an astronomical number, seems not impossible.
This probably requires gathering a country-level amount of magic. Collecting such a huge amount of magic in Equestria or the Changeling Empire will inevitably attract the attention and action of the authorities, and Tirek will notice it. The only place that contains a large amount of magic but is not known to the outside world is the Kirin commune.

Of course, the Kirins will not agree to this absurd cooperation to drain the power of the entire country for a crazy plan with unknown success rate and unknown rewards. Sendak instead proposed to gradually collect magic over three to five years. In exchange, they will teach us dark magic to make up for our lost magic. As for the Kirins’ trade, they will also make up for all the losses — just don’t ask where the money comes from.

§R<=Burn After Reading=>§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_o0]
Agree to Cooperate

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_o1]
Refuse to Cooperate

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12]
Smuggling Case Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_desc]
When the Statistics Bureau summarized and analyzed the internal data of those five years, we found that the total consumption of foal’s breath was relatively normal in other regions, slightly exceeding the standard, but only the §2Eastern Region§! significantly exceeded the standard: the Eastern Region, which accounts for only 15% of the national Kirin population, consumed 40% of the foal’s breath of the entire country!
Why was such an obvious data anomaly covered up? Why was such a large consumption ignored? §2Foal’s breath was smuggled organizationally at scale in the Eastern Region§!, this is our preliminary judgment. And the Eastern Regional government cannot escape suspicion.
The task force immediately dispatched investigators to the Eastern Region, focusing on cities and villages near the southern coast such as Fluttershy Harbour and Seaford for investigation. But strangely — we did §2not§! find any records of large-scale flower exports in §2Fluttershy Harbour§!, nor did we find any smuggling docks or traces.
Is their criminal organization so seamless? Or is there a mole in the investigation team? We need more clues, more evidence. But at least, from the intelligence we currently have, it seems that all provinces in the Eastern Region are involved, with §2Southern Capital§! as the center.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_o0]
Mark as Key Case

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_TOOLTIP]
Unlock a series of decisions: §YSmuggling Key Case§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13]
Smuggling Case Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13_desc]
