[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_23]
Narrow Gate Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_23_desc]
The task force finally made a breakthrough: after checking the goods transfer records in Narrow Gate, we found a huge amount of foal’s breath marked as “used for dealing with Nirik disasters” in Narrow Gate, far exceeding the demand of this remote village. These records also match those of Nan Du.
The task force immediately investigated and interrogated the officials in Narrow Gate. During the investigation, we found that the §2director of the freight office in Narrow Gate, Blossom Burst§!, had serious questionmarks. There used to be a large amount of funds of unknown origin in her account, which have now been spent or transferred. Kirins have also §2witnessed her trading goods with strange Kirins in the border areas§!.
At this point, the mystery of the disappearance of foal’s breath in the Eastern Region has been solved. The task force and the police immediately issued a warrant for the arrest of the director of the freight office, Blossom Burst. However, unfortunately, it seems that she received the information in advance and §2might has already left the Kirin commune territory through Narrow Gate§!.

The smuggling case has been solved, but it does not mean the end of the task force’s investigation.
First, Blossom Burst’s agility made us realize that there are also §2leakers within the task force§!, and we need to carefully investigate all Kirins who have had contact with Blossom Burst.
Second, where did these smuggled foal’s breath eventually go? To the east of Narrow Gate is a vast desert, perhaps we need to cooperate with the Unicornia, Abyssinia, Ornithia and Pirates to have a better chance of catching Blossom Burst.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_23_o0]
File Archived

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_24]
Narrow Gate Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_24_desc]
The task force finally made a breakthrough: after checking the goods transfer records in Narrow Gate, we found a huge amount of foal’s breath marked as “used for dealing with Nirik disasters” in Narrow Gate, far exceeding the demand of this remote village. These records also match those of Nan Du.
The task force immediately investigated and interrogated the officials in Narrow Gate. During the investigation, we found that the §2director of the freight office in Narrow Gate, Blossom Burst§!, had serious questionmarks. There used to be a large amount of funds of unknown origin in her account, which have now been spent or transferred. Kirins have also §2witnessed her trading goods with strange Kirins in the border areas§!.
At this point, the mystery of the disappearance of foal’s breath in the Eastern Region has been solved. The task force and the police immediately issued a warrant for the arrest of the director of the freight office, Blossom Burst. However, unfortunately, it seems that she received the information in advance and §2might has already left the Kirin commune territory through Narrow Gate§!.

The smuggling case has been solved, but it does not mean the end of the task force’s investigation.
First, Blossom Burst’s agility made us realize that there are also §2leakers within the task force§!, and we need to carefully investigate all Kirins who have had contact with Blossom Burst.
Second, where did these smuggled foal’s breath eventually go? To the east of Narrow Gate is a vast desert, perhaps we need to cooperate with the Unicornia, Abyssinia, Ornithia and Pirates to have a better chance of catching Blossom Burst.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_24_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_24_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_25]
Northern Region Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_25_desc]
Though we have little contact with the Kirin to the north, our relationship is not bad, and they also face the threat of Tirek. Therefore, if there is a major smuggling case on the border with the dragons, the dragons should report to us. After all, the dragons are those who love fire and gems, and are not interested in flowers.
After coordinating with the dragons and investigating the border areas, we have ruled out the possibility of the foal’s breath being smuggled out of the country through the northern border.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_25_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_26]
Kirin Forest Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_26_desc]
Kirin Forest is a relatively closed agricultural area. Residents engage in farming, hunting, and gathering activities on a village or even individual basis. Even the local government sometimes finds it difficult to organize the residents. Therefore, initially, the task force believed that Kirin Forest was unlikely to be related to smuggling.
However, during the investigation, we discovered some unusual information: the neighboring country, §2Unicornia§!, has been §2purchasing various flowers in large quantities§! from the market in the past few years, reaching an abnormal level. As a result, the §2Home of Flowers§! in Kirin Forest has received many additional orders, improving the living standards of local residents.
Although we are not yet clear about the motivation of Unicornia to purchase flowers, this is enough to link the foal’s breath smuggling case with Kirin Forest.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_26_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_27]
Kirin Forest Investigation Report

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_27_desc]
Kirin Forest is a relatively closed agricultural area. Residents engage in farming, hunting, and gathering activities on a village or even individual basis. Even the local government sometimes finds it difficult to organize the residents. Therefore, initially, the task force believed that Kirin Forest was unlikely to be related to smuggling.
However, during the investigation, we discovered some unusual information: the neighboring country, §2Unicornia§!, has been §2purchasing various flowers in large quantities§! from the market in the past few years, reaching an abnormal level. As a result, the §2Home of Flowers§! in Kirin Forest has received many additional orders, improving the living standards of local residents.
Although we are not yet clear about the motivation of Unicornia to purchase flowers, this is enough to link the foal’s breath smuggling case with Kirin Forest.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_27_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_27_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_27_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_28]
Archive: Blossom Burst

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_28_desc]
Blossom Burst, the §2former director of the Kirin Commune Freight Bureau§!, once lived in the Peaks of Peril with Autumn Blaze and Rain Shine, but her ancestors are recorded to be from Narrow Gate. After the “Silence” was lifted, due to what was seemingly a political disagreement, she §2resigned from the position of director of the Freight Bureau§! after an argument with Rain Shine, left Peaks of Peril, and §2returned to Narrow Gate§! as the sole director of the Narrow Gate’s local Freight Bureau.
Now we realize that since then, Blossom Burst has been engaged in the smuggling of foal’s breath in Narrow Gate. Even further back, it makes the task force shudder to think: the Blossom Burst in life is a calm and rational Kirin, but the outbreak of the Nirik disaster in the Peaks of Peril, which led to the “Silence”, was caused by an impulsive act of Blossom Burst. Smuggling, resignation, political disagreements, and even that Nirik disaster, are they all part of Blossom Burst’s plan?
What puzzles the task force and Autumn Blaze is that Blossom Burst is not the kind of Kirin who is greedy for wealth. Could Blossom Burst’s §2motive§! for smuggling be simply to retaliate against Rain Shine due to political disagreements? Even Autumn Blaze, who has lived with Blossom Burst for a long time, cannot understand this.
In any case, Blossom Burst’s years of smuggling activities, even if reported by the public, have not been dealt with, which means that every official in the capital Peaks of Peril who has had a past with Blossom Burst may be involved and become Blossom Burst’s protector...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_28_o0]
Things are getting complicated

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_29]
Archive: Blossom Burst

