[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_39_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_40]
Talk Record: Rain Shine

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_40_desc]
As the investigation team was unable to find enough data on that period and on Blossom Burst, Autumn Blaze and the investigation team found the former leader Rain Shine and asked her about the situation at that time.
Rain Shine said that Blossom Burst worked diligently during her tenure as the Director of Kirin Commune Freight Bureau, and she did not notice anything unusual. She also did not believe that Blossom Burst could have been involved in smuggling.
Regarding §2Blossom Burst§!, Rain Shine said she remembered the reason Blossom Burst resigned was because she wanted to return to her hometown to §2take care of her sister§!, rather than the political differences or conspiracies that were rumored. The argument between Blossom Burst and Rain Shine was only because Rain Shine tried to retain her, while Blossom Burst insisted on leaving.
Regarding §2the management of the foal’s breath during the “Silent” period§!, Rain Shine herself did not remember clearly, it might be the responsibility of Nan Du, but she was very uncertain either.
Autumn Blaze showed Rain Shine the talk records of the investigation team with other Kirins. After reading them, Rain Shine believed that these suspects were all §2capable Kirins she had promoted§!, and she §2did not believe that any of them would be involved in smuggling or protecting smuggling§!.
Rain Shine suggested Autumn Blaze to carefully investigate the doubts in the talk records and the §2contradictions in the statements§! of different Kirins, rather than hastily drawing conclusions.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_40_o0]
Thank you, Leader

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_41]
Strange Mail

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_41_desc]
Today, the investigation team received a strange mail. The mail only contained a photo. The photo was very blurry, as if it was taken secretly in the bushes, and you could vaguely see §2two gray Kirins§!, next to them were boxes of goods. The photo was taken at the §2Narrow Gate warehouse§!, where one Kirin was giving a large bag of gold coins to another Kirin — §2Blossom Burst§!. On the back of the photo, there was a line of words, §2“Blossom Burst and Aquamarine, Narrow Gate, 3rd year of ‘Silence’ lift.”§!, with a signature below it, §2“Punjab”§! — obviously a pseudonym. The investigation team verified the authenticity of the photo and confirmed that §2the photo was real§!.
Happening just before the investigation results were announced, this photo completely disrupted the investigation team’s train of thought. Aquamarine claimed in her testimony that she had not met Blossom Burst since she returned to Narrow Gate, but this photo contradicted her words. §2Aquamarine immediately became the prime suspect of the investigation team§!.
However, upon further observation of the details in the photo, the investigation team discovered unusual details. Among the goods in the boxes, most of them were marked with the logo of the §2Freight Bureau§!, but there were also several boxes marked with §2“Fluttershy Harbour”§!.
Who sent this photo? How did they know about the progress of the investigation?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_41_o0]
Things are more complicated than expected

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42]
Blossom Case

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_desc]
Finally, the highly anticipated major foal’s breath smuggling “Blossom Case” has come to an end. Blossom Burst, the Director of the Narrow Gate Freight Bureau, is still on the run, but the larger umbrella behind Blossom Burst has been discovered.
The investigation team announced the investigation results to the public today, and the mastermind behind the scenes is —

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_o0]
Aquamarine

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_o1]
Burnt Umber

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_o2]
Composed

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_o3]
Grass-Green

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_o4]
Ochre

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_42_TOOLTIP]
After selection, the target will be arrested and put on trial. You can view the talk records with each Kirin in the item §Y“Blossom Case” Follow-up Investigation Archives§! in the inventory.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_43]
Aquamarine’s Trial

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_43_desc]
At the very end, the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case” — Aquamarine, was brought to court. The photo received in the final moments became key evidence. Although Aquamarine continued to deny it and claimed that it was a fake photo, this reason did not convince the judge. Testimonies from Rain Shine and Composed showed that Aquamarine was responsible for the transportation of foal’s breath in Nan Du, while Aquamarine insisted that she was not responsible for it. In addition, Aquamarine could not explain her hasty departure from the investigation team’s meeting and her subsequent disappearance.

In the final moments before the court’s verdict, a Kirin broke through the court’s security and entered the courtroom, claiming that Aquamarine was innocent. This was the drama actress who had once starred in “The Phantom of the Opera” with Aquamarine — Chanteuse. She explained to the judge that Aquamarine left the investigation team’s meeting to meet with her, and she could prove that Aquamarine had dinner with her at a restaurant that night. Chanteuse also claimed that she had never heard of Aquamarine’s work being related to foal’s breath when she was with her. Chanteuse insisted that the Aquamarine she knew, was an honest and law-abiding official who could not possibly be involved in smuggling.

However, Chanteuse could not explain the evidence photo, so in the end, the court still ruled Aquamarine guilty and sentenced her to life imprisonment, to be held in the Peaks of Peril Prison. But the secret love affair between Chanteuse and Aquamarine suddenly became the public’s focus, and the limelight even overshadowed the news of Aquamarine’s imprisonment.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_43_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_44]
Burnt Umber’s Trial

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_44_desc]
At the very end, the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case” — Burnt Umber, was brought to court. His nervous attitude during the investigation team’s meeting made him one of the most suspected Kirins. This time, Burnt Umber’s performance in court and in public was not good either, he revealed a lot of his dark history himself, and his relationship with Blossom Burst, who used to be his neighbor, made him even more suspicious. More importantly, after Blossom Burst disappeared, the police searched the entire Kirin Forest and posted wanted posters nationwide, but did not find Blossom Burst. Burnt Umber’s description of Blossom Burst possibly still being in the country seemed like a red herring, deepening his suspicions and reminding the judge of his control over the border inspection forces as a military leader.
Though Burnt Umber continued to deny that he was the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case”, the court still ruled Burnt Umber guilty and sentenced him to life imprisonment, to be held in the Peaks of Peril Prison. There was a lot of disagreement in public opinion on this case, with many Kirins thinking that Burnt Umber was too dull to be the kind of Kirin who could command smuggling for years without being discovered; many others believed that Burnt Umber was indeed guilty. After that, protests and support for the verdict were heard across the country, and Burnt Umber’s case became a hot topic of discussion nationwide.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_44_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_45]
Composed’s Trial

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_45_desc]
At the very end, the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case” — Composed, was brought to court. There were already clues from when she was questioned by the investigation team, she was prepared for the investigation team’s questions, pretended to casually mention Aquamarine, and diverted the entire investigation team’s attention to Aquamarine.
The evidence that ultimately exposed Composed was the photo she sent out in the final moments: Composed was “Punjab”. After talking with Rain Shine, the investigation team learned that Blossom Burst had a sister at home, so even if the photo was real, the content of the photo was actually Blossom Burst and her sister, not Aquamarine. More importantly, Composed took this photo secretly, which became evidence that she, as “Punjab”, had appeared in Narrow Gate.
During the interrogation, Composed’s psychological defense collapsed, and she tearfully admitted to the investigation team that she had framed Aquamarine. Since starring in “The Phantom of the Opera”, Composed had a crush on the actress Chanteuse, but Chanteuse ignored her and started dating Aquamarine instead, which made Composed jealous. When she learned that the “Blossom Case” was investigation was just beginning, she had evil thoughts. However, even though she admitted to framing Aquamarine, she also insisted that she did not participate in the smuggling case or take the photo. Composed claimed that she had never been to Narrow Gate, and she received the photo in an anonymous email, only the line was added by herself. In addition, she never knew that Blossom Burst had a sister.
In the end, the court ruled Composed guilty and sentenced her to life imprisonment, to be held in the Peaks of Peril Prison. The triangle relationship between Composed, Aquamarine, and Chanteuse became a hot topic of discussion nationwide. However, Aquamarine expressed regret over this, and she hoped that the media would stop reporting on this matter to avoid harming Chanteuse, who had nothing to do with this.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_45_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_46]
Grass-Green’s Trial

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_46_desc]
At the very end, the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case” — Grass-Green, was brought to court. The experiment logs he used to prove her innocence became the basis for her conviction: although all the foal’s breath was clearly recorded, the records of other flowers were rather vague.
Grass-Green admitted that he had a secret cooperation with Blossom Burst in Narrow Gate for several years. Although he claimed that it was not related to smuggling, the investigation team and the judge believed that he disguised the foal’s breath as ordinary flowers for smuggling out of the country. Under questioning, Grass-Green was forced to admit that he transported flowers out of the country to Unicornia, but insisted that they were ordinary flowers rather than foal’s breath, and he did not profit from it either.
The judge asked Grass-Green about her motives: why would he, whether it was foal’s breath or ordinary flowers, take the risk of breaking the law and give them to Unicornia for free? Grass-Green remained silent and refused to answer.
In the end, the court ruled Grass-Green guilty. Considering her outstanding contributions to the Kirin agricultural community, the verdict only confiscated all her earnings and temporarily detained her in the Peaks of Peril Criminal Labor Education Center. Grass-Green’s contradictory candor and silence made the verdict a hot topic of discussion nationwide. Opponents believed that he did not deserve a reduced sentence because he refused to answer her motives and cooperate with the investigation; conspiracy theorists believed that there were larger forces behind Grass-Green that prevented her from revealing the truth, and it might even be foreign forces — the high-level officials of Unicornia.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_46_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_47]
Ochre’s Trial

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_47_desc]
At the very end, the mastermind behind the “Blossom Case” — Ochre, was brought to court. The logo of the Freight Bureau on the goods in the Punjab photo, and the inadvertent testimony of Burnt Umber, that “A few years ago, he stole a few fragrant herbs from the Freight Bureau’s warehouse and brought them home to grow.”, both proved that the Freight Bureau was in charge of the transfer of the foal’s breath at that time, which matched Aquamarine’s testimony.
In court, Ochre remained silent, and even showed a disdainful and impatient attitude towards the noisy jury. But when questioned by the court, Ochre did not hide anything:
“So, you were behind the scenes guiding Blossom Burst, planning the smuggling of foal’s breath for several years?” Nod.
“So, were your answers to the investigation team all lies?” Nod.
“Do you have anything else to say? Were you coerced or for other reasons?” Shake head.
Cleanly, the court ruled Ochre guilty and sentenced her to life imprisonment, to be held in the Peaks of Peril Prison.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_47_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_48]
Escape

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_48_desc]
Just under a month after Aquamarine was imprisoned, she escaped, and then disappeared in the Kirin Commune like Blossom Burst. She left no records of leaving the country, especially since the prison where she was held was in the capital, Peaks of Peril. The government immediately blocked this news, and currently, the outside world does not know that Aquamarine has escaped.
We quickly arrested the prison guards who assisted in the escape, and even the warden... The evidence we have now, points to the worst assumption — Aquamarine is still not the biggest boss behind the “Blossom Case”, there are higher-level forces involved...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_48_o0]
What a tangled web

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_49]
Escape

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_49_desc]
Just under a month after Burnt Umber was imprisoned, he escaped, and then disappeared in the Kirin Commune like Blossom Burst. He left no records of leaving the country, especially since the prison where he was held was in the capital, Peaks of Peril. The government immediately blocked this news, and currently, the outside world does not know that Burnt Umber has escaped.
We quickly arrested the prison guards who assisted in the escape, and even the warden... The evidence we have now, points to the worst assumption — Burnt Umber is still not the biggest boss behind the “Blossom Case”, there are higher-level forces involved...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_49_o0]
What a tangled web

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_50]
Escape

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_50_desc]
Just under a month after Composed was imprisoned, she escaped, and then disappeared in the Kirin Commune like Blossom Burst. She left no records of leaving the country, especially since the prison where she was held was in the capital, Peaks of Peril. The government immediately blocked this news, and currently, the outside world does not know that Composed has escaped.
We quickly arrested the prison guards who assisted in the escape, and even the warden... The evidence we have now, points to the worst assumption — Composed is still not the biggest boss behind the “Blossom Case”, there are higher-level forces involved...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_50_o0]
What a tangled web

