Escape

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_52_desc]
Just under a month after Ochre was imprisoned, she escaped, and then disappeared in the Kirin Commune like Blossom Burst. She left no records of leaving the country, especially since the prison where she was held was in the capital, Peaks of Peril. The government immediately blocked this news, and currently, the outside world does not know that Ochre has escaped.
We quickly arrested the prison guards who assisted in the escape, and even the warden... The evidence we have now, points to the worst assumption — Ochre is still not the biggest boss behind the “Blossom Case”, there are higher-level forces involved...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_52_o0]
What a tangled web

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_53]
Investigate Unicornia

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_53_desc]
Following the clues to the border, all the clues seem to point to our ancient neighbor — Unicornia.
In the past few years, Unicornia has been buying a large number of flowers of various kinds on the international market. Even though they are the world’s largest flower-growing country, they not only do not export flowers, but also import a large number of them. Their consumption of flowers is like an angry and greedy Nirik’s demand for combustibles. Although we are not sure why they are buying flowers, why should we care? Unicornia is the largest trading partner of the Kirin community’s economic crops, and their small country seems to have endless wealth to support their continued trade deficit.
This time, involving a smuggling case, we reluctantly chose to intervene and consulted Unicornia on the market situation. Their reply was very straightforward: their goal was to buy as many flowers as possible, and the variety had little impact, so even if it was smuggling and the black market, they had no reason to buy the expensive foal’s breath. So this smuggling case is definitely not related to them.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_53_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_54]
Investigate Ornithia

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_54_desc]
The Ornithia Kingdom in the South is the hometown of Captain Celaeno, who is now the recognized leader of the various pirate organizations that dominate the three oceans. They know every ship that sails the seas and flies the skies, and they can get some information about any ship, where they are going and what they are carrying. Therefore, asking them may help us find the final destination of the foal’s breath.
Unfortunately, although they are our southern neighbors, we do not have much communication with them across the sea. It seems that it takes a lot of patience to make a request to a foreign country. However, in the end, they generously provided us with information: they can confirm that no large-scale foal’s breath has passed under their noses. This also means that the foal’s breath has never left the Kirin community by air or sea.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_54_o0]
Okay

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_55]
Climate Risk Assessment

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_55_desc]
Some meteorological observers who returned from studying abroad in Equestria, together with professional meteorologists we invited from Ponyville, have analyzed the data from several observation stations near the Southern Peaks of Peril and Kirin Isles with us. We have come to the following conclusion:
In the past year, the activity of the Windigos has indeed increased worldwide. When cross-referencing the data from the Kirin commune local areas near the southern Windigo territory with the global data, we believe that the Kirin tribe will be severely threatened by the Windigos in the next one or two years.
The data shows that the impact on the Kirinthal continent is more significant than that on the central Equestria continent. We need to be vigilant and start emergency research on cold protection.
In conclusion, the report believes that the Kirin will soon be severely threatened by the Windigos, and we need to take immediate action.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_55_o0]
I remember the report I read was different from this one.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_59]
Unexpected Guest II

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_59_desc]
At noon, the hurried knock on the door of the capital guard woke up Autumn Blaze, breaking her nap.
“Emergency! There is a new visitor at Applejack Harbour, it’s — it’s —”
Autumn Blaze opened her eyes, stretched lazily, and looked at the flustered guard in confusion, “Who? We don’t work at noon — ”
“— It’s, the second-in-command of the Centaurs, Terek’s brother, Scorpan!”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_59_o0]
“Who?”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_60]
Less Kind Than They Say

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_60_desc]
Soon, Scorpan arrived in front of Autumn Blaze with two gargoyle guards. Just like Sendak, the residents of the Centaur Kingdom always prefer direct dialogue.
“Hello, little Kirin.” Scorpan said expressionlessly. “I know you have been contacting Sendak. I don’t know if you have actually cooperated, or how deep the cooperation is, but you still have a chance to withdraw now.”
“Although I don’t really agree with what my elder brother is doing, he is my brother after all. That Sendak dare to think that I would cooperate with him, that’s just ridiculous.”

Before Autumn Blaze could speak, Scorpan gestured to interrupt her. “Don’t expect anything from me, I am less kind than they say, especially when it comes to my brother.”
After that, Scorpan’s tone suddenly softened: “You have nothing to do with Sendak, I don’t want to see you implicated. You also know my brother’s temper: he doesn’t know this yet, but once I tell him about this, nothing can save you.”
“So, you only have two choices, either you make Sendak disappear immediately, and we can pretend that nothing happened. Or, I will tell my brother everything, and you will be dealt with together with Sendak.”

Scorpan turned and left the treehouse office, leaving Autumn Blaze who said nothing.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_60_o0]
It seems we have no choice

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_60_TOOLTIP]
Cult War

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_60_TOOLTIP_2]
End of the Cult

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_61]
Eureka!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_61_desc]
The Sendak Cult shared to Autumn Blaze a new spell they have mastered: §0Construction Technology I§!!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_61_o0]
Is that... a spell?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_62]
Eureka!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_62_desc]
The Sendak Cult is helping the Kirins with §0Spell Training I§!.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_62_o0]
Hooray for cooperation!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_63]
Eureka!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_63_desc]
Under the guidance of the Sendak Cult, the Kirin community has established the §0General Magic Academy§!!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_63_o0]
You mean those good magic, right?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_64]
Eureka!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_64_desc]
Sendak shared a draft of his upcoming magical masterpiece with Autumn Blaze: “§0Modern Magic Theory§!”.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_64_o0]
Careful, don’t get scooped

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_65]
Generous Cult

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_65_desc]
The Sendak Cult seems to have become quite prosperous lately, and they have shared with us 1800 shares of development bonds to subsidize the Kirins’ expenses in their plans.
Of course, their generosity is not without strings attached: don’t look a gift horse in the mouth.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_65_o0]
Thank you?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_66]
Fluttershy Harbour Factory

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_66_desc]
For better trade with the Sendak Cult, we will open a new factory in Fluttershy Harbour.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_66_o0]
Thank you?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_67]
Small Obstacle

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_67_desc]
As the excavation work goes deeper, more and more ancient crystals are discovered, and their value on the market is getting higher and higher. Batches of crystals are being shipped to Fluttershy Harbour, expecting to get higher prices on the international market. Countless contracts have been signed, even beyond our mining speed. Investments, new mining equipment, and Kirins are pouring in every day.
However, the work of continuing to dig into the depths of the cave has to stop — we have reached the site of the mine disaster that year, where a thick wall formed by magic stands. There are some helmets, pickaxes, and a small memorial stone for the victims at the wall.
Through the translucent magic wall, we can vaguely see the depths of the mine: it is a huge and wide underground space, and you can still see the small buildings, iron rails, and mine carts inside, which are the remaining mine facilities. There are even some trees and bushes that don’t know how to survive in this environment without sunlight, distributed regularly around the buildings.
After the mine disaster that year, Rain Shine sealed the mine with magic here, prohibiting all mining operations. Now we can only let Rain Shine come back and unlock this seal.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_67_o0]
We should talk to Rain Shine

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_69]
Deja Vu

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_69_desc]
Just as Autumn Blaze was coordinating the solution to the problem of the Narrow Gate magic seal and preparing to talk to Rain Shine, an urgent message interrupted all arrangements: more than a dozen of Kirins were reported missing from the mining site! The police have advised Autumn Blaze to immediately order a total lockdown of the crystal mine in the Narrow Gate.
The misfortune of years ago seems to have not left this land of the Narrow Gate, the same crystal craze, the same mining work, the same accident, will the outcome be different this time?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_69_o0]
Things are a bit strange, isn’t it too coincidental?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_72]
Public Pressue: §YWar on Corruption§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_72_desc]
A fatal problem has plagued the Kirins: why did the national “de-Silencing” project, which was originally planned to be completed in three years, take nearly five years? Data shows that the amount of foal breath consumed in the “de-Silencing” project far exceeds the theoretical value.
Are there Kirins who are privately selling foal’s breath for profit during the “de-Silencing” project? More and more gossip is spreading among the Kirins, and the government has never investigated this. Isn’t that suspicious?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_72_o0]
“We will deal with it ASAP”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_73]
Public Pressue: §YFoal’s Breath Disposal§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_73_desc]
During the “de-Silencing” project, foal’s breath was a controlled substance. Now that we no longer need to control all of it, the public is waiting for the government to announce its policy on foal’s breath.
Foal’s breath is a precious flower that sells well in the international trade market, so the public is waiting for the government to announce its policy on foal’s breath for the future.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_73_o0]
“We will deal with it ASAP”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_74]
Archeological Discovery: Gold Bars

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_74_desc]
We found crates of gold bars during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName]... But they don’t look like ancient artifacts...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_74_o0]
This is now national property

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_75]
Archeological Discovery: Ancient Technological Manuscripts

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_75_desc]
We found several ancient books during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which contain information about the technology used by the ancient Kirin civilization...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_75_o0]
Good!

[en.C18_ARCHEOLOGY_TECHNOLOGY_BONUS]
Ancient books

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_76]
Archeological Discovery: Ancient Sociological Manuscripts

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_76_desc]
We found several ancient books during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which contain information about the life and social system of the ancient Kirin civilization...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_76_o0]
Good!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_77]
Archeological Discovery: Cave Paintings

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_77_desc]
We found several ancient cave paintings during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which look very similar to the ones near the Stream of Silence: on the left side of the painting is a Kirin, and on the right side is a Nirik, seemingly recording the process and harm of Nirik transformation.
There is no information beyond our knowledge, but this indicates that the Kirin civilization of all ages will record and emphasize the harm of Nirik in various places.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_77_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_78]
Archeological Discovery: Cave Paintings

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_78_desc]
We found several ancient cave paintings during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which look very similar to the ones near the Stream of Silence: on the left side of the painting is a Kirin, and on the right side is... also a Kirin.
Is this a painting error? Or is it due to the fading of the ancient paintings? It is also possible that it only records the daily life of the Kirin, but why are these two Kirin on the left and right exactly the same? Is it a comic?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_78_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_79]
Archeological Discovery: “Black Sand Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_79_desc]
We found an ancient book during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which seems to come from the era shortly after the war between the Peaks of Peril Kirins and Nan Du Niriks, recording the lives of a group of Kirins who survived on the battlefield. Although it is called the “Chronicle”, the book seems to contain many mythical elements.
In the books’ narrative, the fire continued to burn for a month after the war ended, turning the entire land black... To the east was the more thoroughly burned Nan Du, to the south the weather was turning cold, and black sandstorms blocked their retreat to the west and north. After their food ran out, they were trapped here, waiting for their end.
Just as they were about to give up hope, a mysterious unicorn appeared before them: she did not stop to save these Kirins, but walked out of the flames to the east and straight into the sandstorm to the west, disappearing within. But wherever she passed, countless flowers sprouted from the scorched earth, becoming the Kirins’ food and allowing them to survive.
After the war, the Kirins who settled here established the current Hei Sha Fu, the city on the black sand desert that has now become an oasis. This is probably the main content of the “Black Sand Chronicle”, although the events in it may be only half-true, perhaps the hallucinations of these Kirins in their harsh environment. But this book explains the origin of modern Hei Sha Fu, filling in the gaps in the history of this period for archaeologists.
What is more interesting is that it details the agricultural life of the first generation of Kirins who lived here after the war, including many agricultural techniques, such as how to grow crops on completely scorched land and how to use the unique properties of black sand for agricultural production.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_79_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_79_MODIFIER_TOOLTIP]
The foal’s breath production efficiency of §Yfarm§! is increased by §G10%§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_80]
“Black Sand Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_80_desc]
In the books’ narrative, the fire continued to burn for a month after the war ended, turning the entire land black... To the east was the more thoroughly burned Nan Du, to the south the weather was turning cold, and black sandstorms blocked their retreat to the west and north. After their food ran out, they were trapped here, waiting for their end.
Just as they were about to give up hope, a mysterious unicorn appeared before them: she did not stop to save these Kirins, but walked out of the flames to the east and straight into the sandstorm to the west, disappearing within. But wherever she passed, countless flowers sprouted from the scorched earth, becoming the Kirins’ food and allowing them to survive.
After the war, the Kirins who settled here established the current Hei Sha Fu, the city on the black sand desert that has now become an oasis. This is probably the main content of the “Black Sand Chronicle”, although the events in it may be only half-true, perhaps the hallucinations of these Kirins in their harsh environment. But this book explains the origin of modern Hei Sha Fu, filling in the gaps in the history of this period for archaeologists.
What is more interesting is that it details the agricultural life of the first generation of Kirins who lived here after the war, including many agricultural techniques, such as how to grow crops on completely scorched land and how to use the unique properties of black sand for agricultural production.

§b“Verily, ’twas a day when the heavens were veiled ’i black sands, and lo, a unicorn with a mane of cyan and a horn of pink didst purloin the hallowed earth to withstand the tempest of sand, defying the decree of the spirit. The spirit ordered the demise of the unicorn amidst the Emerald Oasis, yet her command fell upon deaf ears. Then didst the spirit rue her decision, instructing her minions to disperse the earth to reestablish harmony upon the orb.” — Original text of the “Black Sand Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_80_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_81]
“Broken Mountain Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_81_desc]
In the books’ narrative, Tirek, the protégé, and his master, Sendak, became enemies. Tirek went to the Duan Shan to fight against Sendak and his followers. Duan Shan were previously known as the “Peaks of Peril”, but were renamed after Tirek cleaved them in half in a fit of rage, therefore calling “Duan Shan”, meaning “Broken Mountain”.
This battle left a deep impression on the local Kirin residents, to the point where they adapted it into a myth, interpreting the outcome of the battle as a change in the heavens and the earth, believing that Tirek’s power caused the tilt of the heavens and the earth, the movement of the sun, moon, and stars, and the shifting of the river.
Shortly after the destruction of the Kirin civilization in Duan Shan, the Kirin civilizations in other regions also disappeared one after another, and the centaurs replaced the Kirins on this land. This is probably the main content of the “Broken Mountain Chronicle”, a valuable resource for centaur scholars and history enthusiasts interested in learning about the Kirin civilization culture that is on the brink of extinction.

§b“’i days of yore, Tirek and Sendak vied for the throne of kings, and ’i his ire, Tirek didst cleave the Kirins’ Peaks of Peril ’i twain. The pillar of heaven wast rent asunder, and the earthly bond wast broken. The heavens didst lean toward the west and north, thus didst travelling lamp, moon, and stars shift their course; the earth found no fullness to the east and south, thus didst waters rise and dust returneth.” — Original text of the “Broken Mountain Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_81_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_86]
“Northern Nether Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_86_desc]
In the books’ narrative, in the north of the Kirin commune was a mountain called “Scintilla”, which was actually a huge dragon named “Torch”. This dragon was thousands of miles long and can cover the entire sky when flying.
According to our current knowledge of the northern dragon clan, the Kirins who established civilization on the northern border at that time probably merged several different dragon clan leaders into the same mythical creature. However, the fate of these Kirins is more intriguing: living with the fire-breathing dragons for a long time, they thought they were part of the dragon clan, so they no longer resisted the Niriks, but instead worshipped the fire of the Niriks. The tribes that held such beliefs migrated northward after becoming Niriks, eventually disappearing in the territory of the dragon clan. It is said that one of the Niriks, named “Scales”, even once seized the Bloodstone Scepter and became the Dragon Lord.

§b“’i the Northern Nether doth rest a mountain of legend, hight Scintilla. The vastness of Scintilla is shrouded ’i mystery, spanning perchance thousands of leagues; it doth metamorphose into a dragon of dread, known as Torch. The expanse of Torch’s back is veiled ’i uncertainty, stretching mayhap thousands of leagues; when provoked, its wings resemble unto clouds adorning the firmament.” — Original text of the “Northern Nether Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_86_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_87]
“Dark Cloud Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_87_desc]
In the books’ narrative, Kirins have not always been a land-based agricultural civilization since ancient times. On the southern coast, ancient Kirins once established a maritime trade civilization. The Kirins in the south mainly traded with the Ornithia Kingdom, which then transported goods to various parts of the world.
However, the prosperity brought by trade did not last long. One day, the fisherponies at the southern ocean dock discovered a strange celestial phenomenon: the sky above the Ornithia Kingdom was shrouded in thick black clouds, with thunder and lightning. Soon, the Kirins found that Ornithia had stopped trading with the Kirins and lost contact with them. Several ships that set sail to Ornithia to investigate the situation disappeared without a trace after entering the black cloud. The cessation of trade also deprived the once prosperous southern Kirins of their livelihood, and they one by one migrated back to agricultural life.
To explain the strange celestial phenomenon that caused all this, the Kirins in the south created a myth: a god resembling a macaque lived in the sky, presiding over thunder and lightning, and crowned himself as the Emperor. The Ornithia Kingdom incurred retaliation because they angered this Emperor of Thunder. They compiled this myth and the history of that time into the “Dark Cloud Chronicle”, warning future Kirin civilizations of the fragility of trade civilization and promoting the idea of prioritizing agriculture over commerce.

§b“The Emperor of Thunder, dark as the night’s ink, with eyes akin to mirrors reflecting unseen depths. His fur, three feet ’i length, and horns twisted ’i a blend of six creatures’ forms, bore the likeness of a macaque.” — Original text of the “Dark Cloud Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_87_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_88]
“Flower Sea Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_88_desc]
In the books’ narrative, the Kirins living in the Kirin Forest once saw a flower sea in green mountains, where a monster resided. The monster was brownish-yellow all over like a fox. She had nine tails and greedily absorbed the fragrance of the flowers, causing the flowers she absorbed to wither.
However, we have found multiple different versions of the “Flower Sea Chronicle”, each with different descriptions and many similarities. Some versions say that the monster is not entirely brownish-yellow, but a mixture of cyan and pink, and she is not absorbing the flower sea but cultivating it. Some versions believe that the monster is indeed brownish-yellow, but the purpose of absorbing the flower sea is not for her own consumption, but to spread the fragrance of the flowers to the unicorns living in the green mountains. Some versions describe the monster as a tree spirit rather than a fox monster, and its “nine tails” are actually vines. Some versions believe that the monster in the green mountains resembles a unicorn, having two forms like the Kirins, named “Unicorn” when in a good mood, appearing cyan and pink, and emitting the fragrance of flowers; when in a bad mood, it turns brownish-yellow and is named “Nrocinu”, absorbing the fragrance of flowers.

§b“’i  greeny mountains lies a sea of flowers, where dwelleth a beast, its form akin to a fox with nine tails, its voice as a caitiff, gluttonous for flowers.” — Original text of the “Flower Sea Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_88_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_89]
Archeological Discovery: “Northern Nether Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_89_desc]
We found an ancient book during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], which recorded the sights and sounds of the Kirin civilization in the Northern Gate, seems to be a historical witness to the communication between Kirins and the dragons in ancient times.
In the books’ narrative, in the north of the Kirin commune was a mountain called “Scintilla”, which was actually a huge dragon named “Torch”. This dragon was thousands of miles long and can cover the entire sky when flying.
According to our current knowledge of the northern dragon clan, the Kirins who established civilization on the northern border at that time probably merged several different dragon clan leaders into the same mythical creature. However, the fate of these Kirins is more intriguing: living with the fire-breathing dragons for a long time, they thought they were part of the dragon clan, so they no longer resisted the Niriks, but instead worshipped the fire of the Niriks. The tribes that held such beliefs migrated northward after becoming Niriks, eventually disappearing in the territory of the dragon clan. It is said that one of the Niriks, named “Scales”, even once seized the Bloodstone Scepter and became the Dragon Lord.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_89_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_90]
Archeological Discovery: “Dark Cloud Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_90_desc]
We found an ancient book during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], recording a rare history of Kirins: the rise and fall of a rare marine civilization. The decline of civilization caused by strange celestial phenomena is indeed a pity and a conversation topic for the Kirins.
In the books’ narrative, Kirins have not always been a land-based agricultural civilization since ancient times. On the southern coast, ancient Kirins once established a maritime trade civilization. The Kirins in the south mainly traded with the Ornithia Kingdom, which then transported goods to various parts of the world.
However, the prosperity brought by trade did not last long. One day, the fisherponies at the southern ocean dock discovered a strange celestial phenomenon: the sky above the Ornithia Kingdom was shrouded in thick black clouds, with thunder and lightning. Soon, the Kirins found that Ornithia had stopped trading with the Kirins and lost contact with them. Several ships that set sail to Ornithia to investigate the situation disappeared without a trace after entering the black cloud. The cessation of trade also deprived the once prosperous southern Kirins of their livelihood, and they one by one migrated back to agricultural life.
To explain the strange celestial phenomenon that caused all this, the Kirins in the south created a myth: a god resembling a macaque lived in the sky, presiding over thunder and lightning, and crowned himself as the Emperor. The Ornithia Kingdom incurred retaliation because they angered this Emperor of Thunder. They compiled this myth and the history of that time into the “Dark Cloud Chronicle”, warning future Kirin civilizations of the fragility of trade civilization and promoting the idea of prioritizing agriculture over commerce.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_90_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_91]
Archeological Discovery: “Flower Sea Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_91_desc]
We found an ancient book during the archeological process in [FROM.FROM.GetName], compiling a series of sightings of a mythical creature.
In the books’ narrative, the Kirins living in the Kirin Forest once saw a flower sea in green mountains, where a monster resided. The monster was brownish-yellow all over like a fox. She had nine tails and greedily absorbed the fragrance of the flowers, causing the flowers she absorbed to wither.
However, we have found multiple different versions of the “Flower Sea Chronicle”, each with different descriptions and many similarities. Some versions say that the monster is not entirely brownish-yellow, but a mixture of cyan and pink, and she is not absorbing the flower sea but cultivating it. Some versions believe that the monster is indeed brownish-yellow, but the purpose of absorbing the flower sea is not for her own consumption, but to spread the fragrance of the flowers to the unicorns living in the green mountains. Some versions describe the monster as a tree spirit rather than a fox monster, and its “nine tails” are actually vines. Some versions believe that the monster in the green mountains resembles a unicorn, having two forms like the Kirins, named “Unicorn” when in a good mood, appearing cyan and pink, and emitting the fragrance of flowers; when in a bad mood, it turns brownish-yellow and is named “Nrocinu”, absorbing the fragrance of flowers.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_91_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_92]
Fall of the Cult

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_92_desc]
At the gate of the Church, dozens of centaurs in gray cloaks are using black magic to defend against the waves of attacks from the Niriks. More and more centaurs are falling, and under the command of an elder centaur, they enter the Church and seal the gate. Soon, cannon fire and magic missiles are raining down on the walls and stained glass windows of the Church, shattering the marble centaur statues on the roof.
Inside the Church, the elder Sendak takes off his cloak and slams his staff heavily on the ground, and a magic circle quickly covers every corner of the Church. Once the enchantment is complete, all the centaurs inside the Church will be teleported to the port, where he has arranged several ships to take them far away from here. Obviously, the sudden attack by the Kirin commune caught Sendak off guard. Even though he was prepared, Sendak and his guards have been chased by the Kirin and Nirik armies since the war began, and now they finally have a moment of calm to cast the teleportation spell.
Although he is no match for Tirek, Sendak is confident in his black magic power. The Niriks won’t be able to break through the Church protected by his black magic. However, at this very moment, Sendak looks grim, as if he has already sensed some disaster. Although all the centaurs in the Church have received Sendak’s black magic teachings, none of them are qualified to be called Sendak’s “protégé”. Since Tirek betrayed him, he has not trained any protégés until he came here ——
A beam of purple-black flame pierced through the main gate of the Church, igniting everything in its path and heading straight for Sendak, who was about to complete the teleportation. The beam was slightly off target, grazing Sendak’s shoulder and burning his cloak. His staff was shattered into three pieces, and the magic circle was broken. Sendak knew that at this moment, only one possess the power to break through his black magic shield. Sendak opened his eyes, raised his head, and saw the figure at the gate of the Church, where the wooden door has already shattered by the flames.
“So, in the end, you are going to be like him too? Autumn Blaze.”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_92_o0]
I have no choice

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_93]
Sendak’s End

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_93_desc]
“Do you know, Autumn Blaze, for the past few centuries, I have always thought that Tirek, who betrayed me, was my greatest enemy, but now, I don’t think like that anymore.”
“You and Tirek, the most outstanding protégés I have ever trained. Your betrayal, no matter how much I hate it, is proof of my successful training. Even though I no longer have the opportunity to gain the power to control the world, at least I can foresee that you and Tirek will have a place in history book, carrying my name.”
“We are all the same. So, I won’t persuade you anymore.”

“No, I am not the same as you and Tirek.” Autumn Blaze interrupted Sendak. “Everything you did was for your own desire for power, while all I did was to protect the Kirin. Even though we are both users of black magic, the difference between us is huge.”
“Although I don’t want to be your enemy, to be honest, I really don’t want our cooperation to end here. There are still many things we haven’t figured out, like last time.” Autumn Blaze was still talking, but Sendak just stood there, listening. “But at this moment, I have no choice, you must understand that. I won’t regret it. Our relationship is a partnership, not a one-sided effort, so we don’t owe you anything, do we? However, Scorpan only named you, so your followers still have a chance to leave here, you should let them go.”
After the remaining centaur followers walked out of the Church and surrendered to the army outside, Sendak walked up to Autumn Blaze and said:
“Oh, one more thing, ‘The Phantom of the Opera’. Your script was very well-written, I like it very much.”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_93_o0]
I have no choice

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_94]
Log I.1

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_94_desc]
- January 2
Advanced 51 meters. Discovered several crystal mines.
- January 3
Rest.
- January 4
Rest.
- January 5
Advanced 43 meters. Discovered several crystal mines.
- January 6
Advanced 51 meters. Discovered several §2high-quality transparent crystal mines§!.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_94_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_94_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_95]
Log I.2

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_95_desc]
- January 7
Advanced 27 meters. Discovered several high-quality transparent crystal mines and a §2hard and pure white crystal wall§!.
- January 8
Failed to break the crystal wall. Reported one pickaxe damaged.
- January 9
Failed to break the crystal wall. Reported four pickaxes damaged.
- January 10
Rest. This crystal wall seems absolutely unbreakable, even no scratches can be made on it by hitting with hooves, heavy objects, or flames. Correction, §2the crystal wall is absolutely transparent§!, the previously observed white color is a layer of ice on it, with accumulated ash on the ice. After the flame removes the ice, the crystal wall almost becomes invisible, only the reflection of oneself in the mirror. Fantastic.
- January 11
Rest. Will go to another mine tunnel for construction, this wall will be taken over by a §2scientist§! for research.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_95_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_95_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_95_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_96]
Log I.3

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_96_desc]
- January 12
Research log 1: According to the miner’s description, this wall does have the most §2perfect reflection, whether it is light, force, or objects§!. We have never found such a §2hard and smooth§! substance, and I began to doubt that it is not composed of crystals.
- January 13
Research log 2: I used the hardest drill bit currently available, and I could not even produce even a small scratch on it. At the same time, I conducted some optical experiments, and the reflectance was close to 100%, far exceeding our measurement accuracy. However, before further experiments... reported one drill bit damaged.
- January 14
Research log 3: When trying to repair the drill bit, I accidentally approached the wall, and the abnormal phenomenon of the magnet on the repair tool is worth noting. No matter whether I put the south pole or the north pole of the magnet near the wall, it shows a repulsive effect. The substance that makes up the wall may have §2strong diamagnetic§! properties.
- January 29
Research log 4: Voice input test, voice input test, voice input test. Ah! I’m finally back! Thanks to those two ponies! I can’t believe why I managed to keep silent for so long. Now looking back at what I was writing in the experimental log at that time, it seems that Rain Shine’s warning was correct, the Stream of Silence not only makes the Kirins unable to speak, but also §2suppresses our emotions, inhibits the desire to express§!, and even makes my research records so rigid and boring. Did I really wrote these things? Hmm... Anyway, now that I’m the only Kirin here from the Peaks of Peril, who got that breath flower or something, I seem to be a bit out of place here. The Narrow Gate is remote and most Kirins are still living in the “Silence”. If no one is in the mood to talk now, I’ll just record everything I want to say in the experimental log. Now I can finally use voice input, no more writing with a quill, that’s great. Oh, right, the main thing! I almost forgot the previous research on this mirror crystal wall... Strong diamagnetism? Ha, interesting.
- January 30
Research log 5: Voice input test, voice input test, voice input test. I’m talking to myself in the cave, and this wall also has a perfect echo, making it particularly empty here. §2Perfect echo, perfect reflection, perfect hardness, strong diamagnetism...§! Hey, wait, I seem to have a bold guess, let me try it... Yes, this wall also has §2no friction§!. After splashing water, the water droplets will slide straight down, in fact, I should have noticed the dripping on the top of the cave earlier...
This wall is really interesting, which makes me curious about where its boundary is. If we chisel the rocks on both sides, will this wall extend to both sides? At least we have not encountered such a thing on the surface at this location, so it shows that this wall still has a boundary. However, the cost of chiseling the entire boundary is too high, I will try other experiments first.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_96_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_96_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_97]
Log II.1

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_97_desc]
- February 2
Research log 6: Voice input test. Is it because I have been in the cave for too long, or because of loneliness? I just noticed that I am talking more and more to myself in the mirror, as if the other side of the wall is not a mirror image but a real world. Wait... I seem to have never thought of it this way... Ah, I’m such a fool, I just suddenly shouted at the wall: “Are you there? Me on the other side? If you are there, respond to me.” I laughed at myself’s stupidity then, of course. I only heard my own echo. It seems that I’v been alone for too long, I should go out more when I have time.
- February 3
Research log 7: Actually... If the other side of the wall is really considered as §2a world that is completely mirrored to us§!... then everything seems to make sense. The perfect hardness and reflection are because the drill bit and the light rays did not touch a hard wall but ran into another self. Two identical objects are equally hard, so when they collide, they naturally break. So does the light reflect back. Friction is the same, two identical objects move parallel along this non-material plane, which is equivalent to the same object moving, so there is naturally no friction. The diamagnetism can also be explained, it is the repulsion of two magnets with the same pole... Wow! What a bold and interesting guess!
- February 4
Research log 8: I found that I can’t even distinguish between another world and a mirror, §2no matter what I do, the other world will completely mimic my actions§!. Even if I toss a coin countless times, the results on both sides are the same. Please, me on the other side, if you really exist, if you can hear me talking, do something different from me. For our favor.
- February 5
Research log 9: My condition is getting worse. Today when I was talking to the wall, or the plane, a passing Kirin miner heard me. So embarrassing. He didn’t say anything, maybe only because he can’t talk, otherwise, ... Ahhhhh! I really wish there was a crack on the ground I can hide into. Wait a minute, I’m really stupid! Even if the other side is really another me, then since the two worlds are completely symmetrical, §2what I think in my mind, she will also think the same thing§!. So we don’t need to talk at all, we just need to think in our minds... and I will immediately know what she is thinking, because I must be thinking the same thing. Ice cream! Sky! Stream of Silence! Ponies! Hey, she should be thinking about these things suddenly. Anyway, even if the other side is a world that is completely identical to us, what’s the use? We will always do the same thing, and we will never be able to communicate.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_97_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_97_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_98]
Log II.2

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_98_desc]
- February 6
Research log 10: In order to cure my condition of talking to the wall or myself, I raised a pet squirrel — a real one, not the kind that is kept in a cage, just one that I accidentally encountered in the wild. Now I finally have something to communicate with, other than that wall. Today I did more experiments to try to verify my guess, but unsurprisingly, the other side is also doing the same experiments, and the experiments still look like, from an outsider’s perspective, I’m going crazy talking to a mirror. However, it is worth noting that the laws of physics in the other world must be opposite to ours. I tried some clockwise and counterclockwise things, and the other side also mimicked them exactly the same.
- February 7
I have §2submitted my current conclusions about this to the Peaks of Peril§!, and I guess I will be §2transferred from here to help Grass-Green§! with her botanical research. Although these crystal mines are good things, they are not the most urgent needs of the Kirin commune. Rain Shine said that a large amount of that breath flower is needed to lift the Stream of Silence, and the current planting volume of the Kirin tribe is far from enough. All scientists should prioritize helping to improve the yield of that flower. Ah! Just kill me, why botanical research? I’m an experimental physicist, what do I know about botany? Maybe my job then will be to serve tea and water to the team leader Grass-Green.
- February 8
I guess today’s recording will be brief, pack up and get ready to go to the Kirin Forest. Sad news for my little Juliana, we’ve only been together for a few days — oh, Juliana is the name I gave to my little squirrel. Should I take her back with me, or is it better to let her stay here in the wild? What do you think, Juliana? There are many flowers and grasses here in the Narrow Gate, plenty of food for you to eat. While in the Peaks of Peril some Kirins are keeping cats and dogs as pets, which might be dangerous for you. Oh shoot! I’m recording too much again, I have to hurry up and pack. Wait, what was that? Did I just see a §0deep purple rift§! flash across that wall? Emm... must have been my eyes playing tricks on me. Hey! Juliana, where are you going? Come back! Did you see something too? Wait, why does Juliana have no reflection on the wall! I remember she had an image before! Hey! Me on the other side, did you just say: “Why is my Juliana gone?” Wait stop talking, stop, stop, stop! (A long silence)
“Nice to meet you, the other me!”
§b“Hello, the other me!”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_98_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_98_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_99]
Log III.1

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_99_desc]
- June 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
The tunnel has been open for a year and four months, and the secret group has now recruited a total of thirty-two employees, or should I say sixty-four employees? Plus a squirrel, the one that our tunnel’s chief scientist raised. Yesterday, Rain Shine* came to the Narrow Gate by herself and had a friendly talk with Rain Shine’. In addition to determining the next work requirements, they emphasized that the existence of the tunnel must be kept strictly confidential and cannot be known to the outside world. The problem is, even if we lockdown this entire mining area, it’s really hard not to attract public attention with so many employees and material needs for experimental equipment. But no matter how difficult the work is, as the director of the Kirin Commune Freight Bureau and the temporary supervisor of the tunnel project, I will definitely get my duty done as Rain Shine* instructed.
- July 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
This is the month for our first exchange of research results between the two sides after the establishment of the tunnel project: last month, Grass-Green* was researching the hybridization of the breath of foals and wild grass, while Grass-Green’ was researching soil improvement. Now we have better hybrid seeds and improved soil at the same time. In addition, Rain Shine* and I had a secret conversation: I will temporarily resign from the position of the director of the Commune Freight Bureau and take up the position of the director of the Narrow Gate Freight Bureau, so as to stay in the Narrow Gate more naturally and guide this secret tunnel project. Rain Shine* and my successor, Ochre*, will help coordinate the allocation of materials, and I will be responsible for covering up the whereabouts of the materials in the Narrow Gate. Rain Shine* is also unsure how long this task will last, but she promised that the day when the truth of the tunnel is revealed, the Kirins will surely appreciate my efforts. As for now, if anyone asks about the reason for my resignation, I’ll just make up something, like I actually have a sister in the Narrow Gate who needs to be taken care of.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_99_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_99_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_100]
Log III.2

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_100_desc]
- August 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
The tunnel has been open for a year and six months, and it is the first month of my resignation as well as the first month of the “de-Silencing” in the Eastern Region. I was surprised to find that our differences are becoming more and more significant: their foal’s breath production is much lower than ours, so the “de-Silencing” is also much slower than ours. Me and Blossom Burst’ reviewed it, and it seems that the problem lies with the squirrel of the tunnel’s chief scientist, named Julian I guess. When the Silencing was lifted, the visiting pony, Fluttershy, told us that the squirrel is very good at finding the wild fields of foal’s breath. Julian and her squirrel family found countless wild foal’s breath flower fields in the Eastern Region and the Kirin Forest. But there was never a Julian’, so they never found those flower fields. We could send some Kirins there to help them mark those locations, but this will undoubtedly increase the difficulty of keeping the tunnel secret. Let’s give it a try first, and at the same time, the other side will send some miners and farmers to help us supplement the missing Kirin labor. In addition, recently I heard from Grass-Green in the north that our neighbor, Unicornia, is also in a state of flower shortage and needs our help. Maybe we can let the commune’ pay flowers in exchange for our foal’s breath? This way, we can help them and our neighbor at the same time.
- September 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
More and more sightings have begun to appear, and we may have to terminate our assistance to them in finding the foal’s breath. Now their foal’s breath production is still far from enough... It’s not just the lack of flower fields, but also a series of chain reactions: fewer flower fields, thus fewer flower farmers and fewer seeds, thus fewer talking Kirins, thus lower work efficiency, thus slower planting... Further, our situation here is not good either, the Narrow Gate has begun to experience frequent earthquakes. Is it because of the construction of the miners sent from the other side? Or is it the instability of the tunnel itself? If there is a problem with the tunnel, then the Kirins we sent out may all be trapped in that world, so we should withdraw them first. After discussing this decision, the other side doesn’t seem too happy. “Is it our fault that my Juliana disappeared? Should we just endure all this? Don’t forget, you are no different from us! It is OUR changes that have brought YOU differences!” Their tunnel’s chief scientist questioned us like this. I didn’t know what to say, but this also makes me suspect whether the miners from the other side were intentionally trying to cause trouble, wanting to create accidents to distract us? Did they want to slow down our “de-Silencing” speed so that we and they are in the same situation? For a moment, I felt ashamed of the malicious thoughts I had produced, but more of fear, will Blossom Burst’ think the same way? Will she notice that... I don’t trust... me?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_100_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_100_o1]
Next Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_100_o2]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_101]
Log III.3

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_101_desc]
- October 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
Unfortunately, our worst concern has come true. In another earthquake, the mine was buried, and many Kirins died. It took us several days to restore the connection with the other side. This time, many employees had strong opinions, and the situation seemed to be deteriorating. Fortunately, after Rain Shine*’ arrived here and held about four negotiations, an agreement was finally reached. Both sides will share the research progress. We will be aiding them with foal’s breath while they will provide us with ores, flowers, and gold coins, etc., as an exchange. Although the mine disaster was tragic, it also brought an opportunity: Rain Shine* had a legitimate reason to announce the blockade of the Narrow Gate. Our tunnel project team can finally operate in complete secrecy without worrying about being discovered. Next, Rain Shine* plans to go abroad to visit Celestia*: Celestia* is a unicorn living on the continent on our west. Just like Rain Shine* leads us, Celestia* is the leader of those ponies. I have to admit that ponies, especially unicorns, have a much better understanding and research of magic than us. Maybe Celestia* will have a better understanding of this tunnel.
- November 9
§R<=TOP SECRET=>§!
Rain Shine* has returned from Equestria, and it seems that she didn’t get any useful information. Celestia* also doesn’t know much about this tunnel. However, after Celestia* learned about our mine disaster, she said that she had encountered the same thing: her student, a princess named Twilight Sparkle*, once went to another world and met another self of the species called “human”. It is said that spatial instability can be caused if many selves from different worlds exist in the same world at the same time. So the mine disaster may indeed have been caused by the miners from the other side, but not intentionally. It was because of the simultaneous existence of both sides.
Rain Shine* also brought back some news about Equestria — the situation over there doesn’t seem optimistic. Celestia* is about to abdicate soon, and Twilight Sparkle* is about to succeed. Equestria seems to be on the brink of some kind of civil war: unicorns, pegasi, and earth ponies are all hostile to each other, and Canterlot is in chaos. Equestria is the enlightener and mentor of friendship of the Kirins, and the current situation they are facing is indeed worrying. Rain Shine* said that the Kirins should avoid being involved, and we will remain vigilant.
Regarding the tunnel, the research cooperation between the two worlds is progressing rapidly. It is expected that we will be able to complete the “de-Silencing” work in both worlds in just three to five years. Our group has officially been renamed as the “Culanika Lokadhātu Undercover Bureau”, or “The CLUB”, directly under Rain Shine’s secret leadership. In the ruins of the mine disaster, a new underground building — the “Lokadhātu Office” — has been constructed. Rain Shine has also established local CLUB secret branches in Peaks of Peril, Nan Du, and the Kirin Forest, mainly infiltrating the Bureau of Freight and the Police Department, ensuring our material supply and confidentiality matters here.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_101_o0]
I’m Done

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_101_o1]
Prev Page

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_102]
Search for the Missing Miners

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_102_desc]
It has been a month, and it can be said that the missing miners have probably all died, unless —
The epicenter of the earthquake is close to the magic seal we discovered at the time. After we dug out the collapsed tunnel, the magic seal and the building inside were still intact. This means that if they somehow entered the seal, they might still be alive.
Perhaps, preventing the earthquake from destroying the buildings in the underground mine itself was one of Rain Shine’s purposes for setting up this seal? Then maybe we shouldn’t ask Rain Shine to lift this seal — if we had lifted this seal earlier, the entire area might have been destroyed by the earthquake.
While hesitating, Autumn Blaze received a report that near the magic seal, the rescue team dug out a part of a dilapidated log. It looks like it was left by a miner, and there seems to be a scientist there, but the time of the log doesn’t seem to match...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_102_o0]
Huh?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_103]
Jailbreak Investigation

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_103_desc]
After Blossom and her accomplices disappeared one after another, the investigation team lost direction. Helplessly, the investigation team returned to the Narrow Gate, Blossom’s hometown, hoping to find some clues.
Rain Shine once told us that Blossom resigned and returned to the Narrow Gate because she had a sister, and the photos of Punjab seemed to prove this. However —— when the investigation team inquired with the local residents, they found that Blossom had never had a sister in the Narrow Gate.
Just as the investigation team was in trouble, a logbook was found in Blossom’s home. The logbook was personally used by Blossom and encrypted with Blossom’s own magic. Although it may contain important clues, we need Blossom’s magic to decrypt it.
This logbook may contain the key to solving all the puzzles that trouble the investigation team. Too bad we don’t have the means to open it yet.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_103_o0]
Huh?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_107]
Among Us

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_107_desc]
Originally, this was just a small mistake in the statistical data: the rate of Kirins and Niriks summed up to more than 100% in some regions. But when an inadvertent investigation began, the Kirins suddenly found that everything started to lose control.
First, at the Bureau of Statistics, the original data of the Eastern Region and Kirin Forest were checked to be true, which meant that there was a problem in the poll stage.
Next, some terrifying records caught the attention of the Kirins: all the Kirins that were double-counted had long been dead, some for more than a year, and some for four or five years.
Then, the investigation team asked some grassroots pollsters, who swore by their reputation and life that they had never double-counted, let alone counted Kirins who had already died...
Then, the police arrested several Kirins who had been registered as “dead” several years ago. Their identity documents, photos, and other information were all proven to be true, and they can also use magic normally. Only the archives showed that they had died many years ago.
Finally, under interrogation, a strange name that repeatedly appeared caught the attention of the investigation team: “The CLUB”. It seems that all the Kirins who were mistakenly considered dead were members of “The CLUB”, and they claimed that the CLUB is just a sobriety mutual aid group...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_107_o0]
Changeling Spies?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_108]
The CLUB

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_108_desc]
So far, we have raided several basements, arrested several members of “The CLUB”, but have not found their leader, or evidence that they are engaged in Changeling spy activities. Our arrests and investigations are currently being conducted in secret to avoid alerting the members of “The CLUB”, but if we continue to find nothing, perhaps we need to publicly announce the existence of this suspected spy organization.
However... as if by coincidence... just as Autumn Blaze was drafting a notice to arrest all members of “The CLUB” within the country and let Kirins keep an eye out —— the latest action report was placed on her desk.
It seems like it was intentional, our previous fruitless investigation has finally made some progress. In the recent raid, we found some magic-related passwords and CLUB files, which seem to be evidence for conviction... but these documents show that they have nothing to do with Changelings.
“The CLUB”, or the “Culanika Lokadhātu Undercover Bureau”, seems to be a “inner circle” within the Kirin commune government. The CLUB’s tentacles have reached various fields, including freight, police, diplomacy, science, construction, agriculture... Who is the core leader of this club?

Wait, among them... we found the password of Blossom Burst... Is Blossom Burst also a member of “The CLUB”?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_108_o0]
Huh?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_108_TOOLTIP]
We obtained §YBlossom Burst’s magic password§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_109]
The Inner Circle

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_109_desc]
When we found Grass-Green again, he readily admitted that he knew about the existence of this so-called “club”, but he was not a member of it. “I am just an agricultural expert, a botanist, or a scientist, I am not qualified to be a member of the ‘Inner Circle’. But because of foal’s breath, the ‘Inner Circle’ often asks me for help.”
When Autumn Blaze asked Grass-Green who the leader of the “Inner Circle” was, Grass-Green remained silent for a long time without answering. Then, he suddenly began to discuss botanical issues with Autumn Blaze: “When you see a blossom bud open, do you ever wonder where its nutrients come from?”
Autumn Blaze was puzzled by the sudden question, but Grass-Green continued: “You might suspect the stems, but they are only responsible for transportation; you might suspect the roots, but they are only responsible for construction; you might suspect the leaves, but they are only responsible for protection. You might even suspect grass around it, but they have nothing to do with the blossom bud.”
Autumn Blaze seemed to understand: “You mean... the nutrients do not come from any of them, but from all of them working together? Wait, we have investigated all of them, and no official has the ability to infiltrate so many departments at the same time, and organize these Kirins togther to commit —”
“No,” Grass-Green interrupted Autumn Blaze, §2“The nutrients for plant growth eventually come from the sun high in the sky, which is now setting in the dusk. That’s why you didn’t notice her. Or, you have become accustomed to the shine, so you deliberately ignored her?”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_109_o0]
... How could it be... Rain Shine?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_109_TOOLTIP]
We obtained §YGrass-Green’s magic password§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_110]
The Inner Circle

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_110_desc]
After the smuggling key case was solved, Blossom Burst and Grass-Green disappeared one after another. After the investigation into the “Inner Circle” came to a standstill, the investigation team came to Grass-Green’s residence once again. Here, the investigation team found a logbook of Grass-Green.
However, what was strange was that this logbook not only used Grass-Green’s own magic encryption, but also the aura of another Kirin — a kind of aura that Autumn Blaze was extremely familiar with.
In the flowerpot, the investigation team actually found Grass-Green’s notes, which recorded several magic passwords, but none of them could unlock the logbook. The investigation team then realized that Grass-Green was not part of the “Inner Circle”: the magic left by Grass-Green on the logbook was not for encryption, but for his attempts to decrypt this logbook.
In other words, Grass-Green, like the investigation team, was also looking for clues to the “Inner Circle”. So he was framed as the mastermind of the smuggling case because of the investigation? Then how did he escape from prison? We don’t know, the only thing we know is a riddle left by Grass-Green:

“When you see a blossom bud open, do you ever wonder where its nutrients come from?”
“You might suspect the stems, but they are only responsible for transportation; you might suspect the roots, but they are only responsible for construction; you might suspect the leaves, but they are only responsible for protection. You might even suspect grass around it, but they have nothing to do with the blossom bud.”
§2“The nutrients for plant growth eventually come from the sun high in the sky, which is now setting in the dusk. That’s why you didn’t notice her. Or, you have become accustomed to the shine, so you deliberately ignored her?”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_110_TOOLTIP]
We obtained §YGrass-Green’s magic password§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_111]
“Tea Party”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_111_desc]
All the intelligence currently available points to the former leader Rain Shine. The most likely explanation for all the mysteries is: former leader of the commune, Rain Shine, during her tenure, formed an “inner circle” with several bureau directors and established “The Club”. Blossom Burst, a memeber of the club, smuggled large amount of foal’s breath from the Eastern Region through the Narrow Gate, under the protection of Rain Shine and Ochre. To cover up of their crimes, Rain Shine used magic to create a protected space in the underground mine of the Narrow Gate, and covered up the existence of this space through a mining accident, using it as a base for a series of smuggling activities. Grass-Green is not a member of the club, but has frequent contact with the club. That’s how the club infiltrated the Science Bureau and conducted secret research. After the “Blossom Burst Smuggling Case” was solved, the club member Burnt Umber used his relationships and influence in the military and police to plan an escape. After the reopening of the Narrow Gate mine, the club planned the disappearance of the miners again to ensure that the magic seal of the underground space was not lifted. To cover up the club’s activities, the lower-level members of the club were all modified in the files as “dead” to escape the police investigation. All of this was instructed by the leader of “The Club”, the former leader of the Kirin commune, Rain Shine.
When the police and the investigation team arrived at Rain Shine’s home, she seemed to be prepared, she directly admitted all the crimes and expressed her willingness to cooperate with the investigation team. Her attitude confused the investigation team. Soon, Rain Shine was taken away.

The police did not arrest Rain Shine, only “inviting her to a tea party at the police station” for questioning. But even though the investigation team and the police kept a low profile, and Rain Shine herself did not make any resistance, the news quickly spread somehow. “Rain Shine may be the mastermind of the ‘Blossom Burst Smuggling Case’? Is it a crackdown on corruption or political persecution?” This news caused a huge stir in the commune. After all, there are still too many unsolved mysteries in the case: where did the foal’s breath go? What do the bilateral exchanges and strange symbols and names in Blossom Burst’s logbook mean? Who are the members of The Club? And the biggest question in the questioning, which the investigation team and Autumn Blaze have not been able to understand: what is Rain Shine’s motive?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_111_o0]
Many questions remain

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_111_TOOLTIP]
We obtained §YRain Shine’s magic password§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_112]
Where Flowers Wither

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_112_desc]
“Here you are, Autumn Blaze.” Rain Shine stood inside the interrogation room, turning around to face Autumn Blaze who had just walked in. Perhaps out of respect for the former leader, the guards did not choose to hoofcuff her.
“Leader, I have read your logbooks. So, you did everything for the other world? Organizing the club, tampering with the statistics, smuggling foal’s breath —”
“I didn’t smuggle, I just provided foal’s breath to the other world as agreed.” Rain Shine interrupted Autumn Blaze.
“I believe you, Leader. But, why? Why did you do all these?” Autumn Blaze looked at the former leader in confusion.

“‘I will do my best to mediate the conflict and avoid unnecessary casualties.’ Autumn Blaze, I still remember, that’s what you said back then.” Rain Shine looked at Autumn Blaze, as if she had returned to that afternoon of succession.
“I did my best to mediate the conflict between the two worlds, because, they are us too.” Rain Shine paused for a moment, as if choking, and then continued to explain: “They conducted meteorological observations more than a year earlier than us, and the result is the report you see now. We have never tampered with the report but only brought the report from the other world. The climate in their world is much colder than ours, and the Windigo has already devoured their Unicornia, sieging their commune, ready to destroy their homeland at any time. So I used my influence to contact Grass-Green and the Science Bureau to help them conduct emergency cold protection research.”
“After returning from Celestia, before the Ultimate Battle, I learned that conflict and disharmony were the source of the intensified Windigo activity. Due to the lack of foal’s breath and lesser use of Stream of Silence, the Niriks rate was much higher than ours. That’s why I arranged Blossom Burst to provide foal’s breath to them.”
“The members of Culanika Lokadhātu that you arrested, their ‘deaths’ were not a file tampering either. They came from the other world. Those memebers in our world died in accidents, and they crossed the tunnel to voluntarily help maintain contact between the two worlds.”

After a long silence, Rain Shine seemed to return to that afternoon again, when she gave a foal’s breath to Autumn Blaze and gently said to Autumn Blaze:
“I have made an irreparable mistake, and nothing can clear my sins. I’m sorry, Autumn Blaze.”
Autumn Blaze once thought it was about ‘Silence’, but now she understood that it was about the tunnel and Culanika Lokadhātu.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_112_o0]
This is not a sin

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_113]
Where Flowers Wither

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_113_desc]
“Thank you, Leader. I can understand everything you did. If this is the ‘sin’ you mentioned when you gave me the foal’s breath, then I think you shouldn’t be punished for it. We will explain everything to the public, and you should be acquitted —” Before Autumn Blaze could finish, Rain Shine closed her eyes, turned her head away, looking very disappointed and heartbroken.
“No, I am guilty.” Rain Shine said slowly, “I am guilty, and that’s why I have to abdicate.”

“In years of contact, I once had a thought — what if, no matter how much effort we put in, their homeland is still devoured by the Windigo? When I had this thought, the other side, or Rain Shine-Prime, would naturally think the same. We tried to set up a refugee camp in the tunnel, which is now the Lokadhātu Office, where the missing miners are. That earthquake killed all our hopes of coexistence — if the same individual from different worlds appears in the same world at a large scale, the whole world will collapse in instability, just like those earthquakes. So —”
“In the dilemma, I had the idea of strengthening the army to defend against the other side: if the Windigo invaded them, in desperation, they may try to kill us and seize our world. Even though I regretted it in an instant, I realized that Rain Shine-Prime had already had the same idea. From that moment on, everything was irretrievable.”
“Their transition of power was a few months earlier than ours. At that time, Rain Shine-Prime chose to abdicate and let Autumn Blaze-Prime lead their commune. So when I learned that your answer, Autumn Blaze-Asterisk, was ‘if it is inevitable, I will let the Kirins take up arms’, I knew the choice of Autumn Blaze-Prime. In despair, for the survival of their commune, their Autumn Blaze-Prime would choose to take up arms. The war between the two worlds has become inevitable.”

“You mean, Autumn Blaze-Prime has already chosen war, so I must also choose war.” Autumn Blaze looked at Rain Shine, suddenly at a loss. “If that’s the case, why didn’t you come to me and explain everything to me at the very beginning?”
“Rain Shine-Prime and I made an agreement to prevent the existence of the tunnel from being known to the public or the outside world. I must abide by the agreement, otherwise, she would naturally tell her Autumn Blaze-Prime about all this, and the war would come even earlier.” Rain Shine sighed, “I still harbor an unrealistic fantasy, that every other day I can delay, there will be more chances to save them. We have been risking the exposure of the Culanika to help them research cold protection technology, but we just don’t have enough time. The Autumn Blaze-Prime on the other side is as smart as you, and their investigation is as fast as yours. At the time you took me here, I received a final message from Culanika — the other side has closed the tunnel and no longer responds to any of our messages.”

“This means they have begun to prepare for the final war.” Autumn Blaze also lowered her head, sighing softly.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_113_o0]
‘If it is inevitable, I will let the Kirins take up arms.’

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_114]
Lokadhātu War

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_114_desc]
“If it is inevitable, I will let the Kirins take up arms. The Kirins will survive, even if it means that some of us, or even I myself, become Niriks or die on the battlefield, even if it means facing my former fellows and dear friends with arms, I will choose to do so.”

In the end, Autumn Blaze’ from the other world resorted to force. In the face of survival, Autumn Blaze* believes that she would make the same choice. Whose fault is the war? This is no longer important.
Regardless of who is the winner, they will carry the history and reincarnation of the Kirins for thousands of years, and will continue to survive on this land.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_114_o0]
War does not determine who is right, only who is left.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115]
Winner Takes All

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_desc]
The war between two worlds has ended, the winner will take all, and the loser will lose everything... right? At this moment, Autumn Blaze* and Autumn Blaze’ are staring at each other, they both know that there is one last stroke of the war: the winner will decide the fate of the loser.
Celestia once warned us: when the same individual from different worlds appears on the same world on a large scale, the entire world will collapse in instability. The numerous earthquakes in the history of Narrow Gate have proven this point, and this is also the starting point for us to go to war with ourselves.
So, how will the winner choose? Will the loser be driven to that world, to survive and die in the ice and snow under the howling Windigos? Or will they be sheltered in this world, facing the unknown instability and the collapse of the world with us?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_o0]
We will honor the result of the war

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_o0_TOOLTIP]
They are not us. We will expel them to another world, let them survive and die on their own. Because although we sympathize with their suffering, coexistence will only lead to instability, and their failed aggression has made the choice of who can survive.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_o1]
We will face the challenge together

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_o1_TOOLTIP]
They are us. We will shelter them, but the world may be destroyed because of this. Although history has proven that coexistence will lead to instability and disaster, we do not believe that this is inevitable. We should fight against disasters together instead of abandoning them to feed the disaster.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_115_THREAT]
They Are Not Us

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_116]
Nightfall

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_116_desc]
Any sane Kirin should understand by now that this civilization has once again reached the final moment of her life. The Niriks are rampant, the original social organization has completely failed, and the entire community is slowly collapsing and disintegrating.
Maybe, we still have a chance to leave something behind: in the entire history of Kirins, such a cycle is not uncommon, but this is the first time that an organization has lasted for decades nationwide. We established contacts with Equestria, we established contacts with the Dragons and Unicornia. They will witness our doomsday, and they will witness our rebirth.
So let’s start writing again, using flames to melt the rocks, and writing our story on them stroke by stroke: ... from the stars there then reached down the heavenly flame, and where it touched, the citis of Peaks of Peirl flamed to utter destruction, so that of Kirins and of the works of Kirins nought remained.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_116_o0]
May we meet again in the next cycle.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_117]
“Burning Sky Chronicle”

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_117_desc]
In the books’ narrative, to face the disaster, the Kirins bravely transformed into Niriks, but these Niriks became the enders of civilization. We are not sure if they won the war, but that does not matter anymore.
For the first time, an organization lasted for decades nationwide. They established contacts with Equestria, they established contacts with the Dragons and Unicornia. The outsiders witnessed their doomsday, and also witnessed our birth.
Perhaps, openness itself was a mistake? Or perhaps, even in the “Silence” they could not avoid the same fate?

§b“Standing towards the top of peaks of peril and beholding the vista, the edifices were engulfed ’i flames. The splendor of yore hath faded into oblivion. Naught remaineth yet the meager verdure, and the meandering waters.” —— Original text of “Burning Sky Chronicle”§!

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_117_o0]
Interesting

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_126]
Friendship with Unicornia

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_126_desc]
After contacting the unicorn sanctuary, they offered to help us build factories and infrastructure in exchange for our plant resources.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_126_o0]
Mutual Benefit

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_126_o1]
Next Time

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_127]
Friendship with Dragons

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_127_desc]
Unlike us Kirins, the Dragons are not good at producing things. They mostly rely on scavenging, plundering and trading for their daily necessities. They have a lot of gems but lack food and clothing.
They hope that we can exchange our crops, textiles and handicrafts for their gems and other precious items.
In addition, by the way, the Dragons are very good at training warriors.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_127_o0]
Mutual Benefit

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_127_o1]
Next Time

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_128]
Friendship with Resistance

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_128_desc]
Dealing with the Resistance should be done with caution, as we do not want to offend the upholders of order: the Empire, the Shapeshifters and the Centaurs.
Therefore, we will not provide any military support to the Resistance, but they are willing to train our troops in the use of modern firearms for free.
They only ask that we secretly disclose some information to them when trading with those Imperial officials.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_128_o0]
Mutual Benefit

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_128_o1]
Next Time

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_128_TOOLTIP]
Friendship with Resistance

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_129]
Friendship with Ornithia

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_129_desc]
Ornithia has invited us to join their pirate fleet to explore uncharted waters and search for legendary treasures...
Uh... What treasures? Are these “treasures”... legal?

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_129_o0]
Mutual Benefit

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_129_o1]
Next Time

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_129_TOOLTIP]
Assemble the Kirin Bao Chuan Fleet in §Y[184.GetName]§!.

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_130]
“Friendship” with Ornithia

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_130_desc]
When our Kirin envoys, after layers of disguise and protection, entered the territory of the Equestria Empire and found those high-ranking officials who had once done business with us, they seemed to misunderstand our intentions.
Every time we entered a house, when our envoys expressed to them, “The Kirin had a very pleasant cooperation with you last time, and we hope to further contact the Empire”, they always seemed very flustered and asked us what we wanted.
In the end, the result was often that they gave us a lot of development bonds, only asking us not to mention their transactions with them to any pony else... After making a round trip in Canterlot, we have already obtained at least half a month’s trade revenue...

[en.EVENT_C18_MAIN_130_o0]
Okay

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1]
传承

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1_desc]
“新元年”的第二天，得知消息的麒麟国就也发生了一件大事：雨晴向麒麟们宣布，她将退位，将麒麟领袖的职责禅让于最出色的麒麟——秋烨。
虽然雨晴的退位是标志着重要的改变，但麒麟国早已做好了准备。几个月来，雨晴已经开始逐渐减少自己的公开活动，将更多的事务交给秋烨处理。秋烨也在这段时间里展现出了自己的能力，让麒麟们对她的领导能力有了更多的信心——更不如说，原本麒麟们就已经将这个解除全麒麟静默的最大功臣视为未来的领袖。
雨晴表示，“新元年”的发生的确令她始料未及，但她的退位与“新元年”并无直接关系，毕竟遥远的麒麟索尔大陆受到的影响并不大：“我是一位和平主义者，但我也是一位现实主义者。我知道，如今的世界形势正在发生变化，麒麟国也在这几年间愈加开放。我相信，在这样一个动荡而又充满挑战的年代，充满活力的秋烨，相比于追求稳定的我，更能带领麒麟国走向未来、抓住机遇。”
另一方面，雨晴也表示，自从声音恢复以后，她就一直想要再演艺事业上复出。
“曾经我是一名领袖，但此后我想重新做回一名歌手。” 雨晴如是说。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_1_o0]
欢庆，欢庆

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2]
鲜花盛开之处

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2_desc]
“你来了，秋烨。” 雨晴站在花园的露天阳台上，转过身来面对着刚刚走进来的秋烨。
秋烨走到雨晴身边，抬头看向雨晴。还没等秋烨说什么，雨晴再次开口：“明天开始，这里就属于你了。但在此之前，我还有一个问题要问你。”
这似乎是即将卸任的领袖为接任者秋烨准备的一道测试题，秋烨尊敬地点了点头，示意雨晴继续。

“假如有一天，逆麟再次出现在这片土地上，你会怎么做？”
秋烨立即回答道：“领袖，我认为我继任后的最重要任务就是避免这种事情再次发生。”
“不，假如已经发生了，没有挽回的余地。为了麒麟族的生存，你将不得不与自己的同胞兵戎相见，此时你会怎么做？” 雨晴立即否定了秋烨的回答。
沉默良久，秋烨迟疑着回答道：“我会尽我所能调停冲突，避免无谓的伤亡。但如果这是不可避免的，我会让麒麟们拿起武器。麒麟族将要生存下去，即使这意味着我们的一部分，甚至我自己变成逆麟或者在战场上牺牲，即使这意味着与昔日的同胞和挚友兵戎相见，我也会选择这样做。”

听完，雨晴立即闭上了眼，将头转过身去，似乎十分失落、痛心。秋烨看着雨晴的背影和神情，小心翼翼地问：“所以，领袖您认为我做出了错误的选择么？您希望我做出怎样的选择？”
难道领袖希望我们放下武器投降吗？或是被那些疯狂的逆麟们所屠戮？秋烨心中疑惑，但却没有说出口。
雨晴却只是摇摇头：“不，这个问题并没有答案。我只是想听到你的想法而已。” 看着秋烨不解又带有少许担忧的表情，雨晴继续说道：
“秋烨，你已经做出了你的选择，那就没有退路了。继任后，请认真为即将到来的战争做好准备吧。”

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_2_o0]
“什么？”

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3]
气候风险评估

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3_desc]
一些从小马利亚留学回来的气象观测员，与我们从小马谷请来的专业气象学家共同分析了险崇峰南麓与麒麟群岛的若干观测站数据，我们得出结论：
在过去的一年中，风之魔的活动在全世界范围内确实有所提升。然而交叉对比靠近南部风之魔领地的麒麟社群地区数据与世界范围数据，我们并未发现显著区别。
这意味着，风之魔的活动增加并未给麒麟族带来额外的降温降雪或者任何气候风险。相比之下，数据表明海马利亚与克鲁格镇等地区具有更加严重的降温趋势，相关方更加有必要保持警惕。
综上所述，报告认为麒麟目前并未受到气候风险的威胁，但是面对一个全球性的气候变化，我们与其他国家仍然需要一同保持努力。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_3_o0]
好吧

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4]
稚马狂热

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_desc]
在初步的对外开放中，我们发现所有出口的商品中，我们的特产花朵“稚马之息”在国际市场上最受欢迎。这种散发着淡淡清香的花朵，还有提神醒脑的功效，可以让使用者思考迅速，语言流畅。
不同于外界所认为的高档装饰花卉，“稚马之息”对于麒麟们来说是重要的战略物资 —— 解除“静默”的唯一解药。长久以来，因为解除“静默”所需要的“稚马之息”数量巨大，政府严格限制了其出口，以优先保证国内的供应，这进一步推高了“稚马之息”的价格。
如今，在全国范围内的“静默”已经被成功解除，“稚马之息”不再是我们的必需品，而全国还有无数的种植园正在种植这种花朵。也许是时候放开这一限制，让更多种植“稚马之息”的农民改善生活了。
不过，专家提醒，全面放开“稚马之息”的出口反而会导致其价格下跌，种植利润降低。我们可能需要更加谨慎地考虑这一点。
除经济之外，一个更重要的担忧是：半人马此前对我们兴趣不大，在他们的刻板印象中，麒麟社群不过是丛林中的未开化部落罢了。这也是为什么终末之战后我们有幸逃过了半人马的绝大部分压榨。但当“稚马之息”在半人马上层贵族中兴起热潮时，我们是否会招来提雷克的注意呢？

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o0]
全面允许自由出口

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o1]
放松出口管制

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_4_o2]
保持现状

[zh.C18_DRAW_ATTENTION_1_TOOLITP]
我们§Y可能§!会吸引 §R[C22.GetName]§! 的注意。

[zh.C18_DRAW_ATTENTION_2_TOOLITP]
我们很§Y可能§!会吸引 §R[C22.GetName]§! 的注意。

[zh.C18_LESS_ATTENTION_1_TOOLTIP]
我们将更加不容易被 §R[C22.GetName]§! 注意。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8]
不速之客

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8_desc]
苹果嘉儿港的集市是麒麟社群中最热闹的地方，甚至超过了首都险崇峰。在这里你能看到各种各样的麒麟、小马、狮鹫、化茧幻形灵，甚至还有一些偷偷来销赃的帝国官员。
商船进进出出，每一艘都意味着数不尽的财富和机会。相比于叫卖吆喝的声音，这里你更常听到的是金币从袋中倾泻而出、发展债券被拍在木头桌子上、货物从木船上滑下、成交后老板们击蹄、拍肩或是点燃烟斗的声音。一次这样的交易，对于麒麟之森的那些独居麒麟来说，可能就是一生的财富。

隐匿在穿行的巨型货船之间，一只小木船悄悄地靠岸。几只身着斗篷，完全看不见面相的小马从船上走下，自动排成了两列，跟随着他们的领头者——一只拄着拐杖的斗篷小马，向码头更远的集市走去。一路上，他们时不时驻足观看，看着那些老板叼着烟斗靠在货物上，与本地的麒麟们谈着生意。不过，他们似乎更关心的，是那些用他们发着光的角搬运货物的年轻麒麟伙计。斗篷队伍最终在集市里的一家小门店前停下，这里的招牌是“麒麟搬运”。
领头者站在门口用拐杖敲了两下地，听到声音，一位麒麟店老板很快就开门迎了上来。看到后面的斗篷小马们，她的生意眼睛立刻亮了起来：“哟！这么大的阵仗！一瞅就是外地来的大老板！您有不少货要搬吧？我们店里的小伙子，魔力都是麒麟族里面顶尖的，几艘船的货物，几个小时就能搬完！看您是大老板，以后和我们小店长期合作，我给您打个折吧！您看怎么样？我们在全国都有分店，就算您去柔柔港或者是险崇峰，我们都能给您提供最好的服务！”

从斗篷下那深邃不可见的黑暗中，领头者苍老而又厚重的声音终于响起：“魔力？看来很符合我的期待。” 领头者缓缓摘下斗篷的兜帽——
是一只半人马。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_8_o0]
警戒！

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9]
警戒

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9_desc]
在店主慌张地敲钟报案后，集市巡逻队很快来到了“麒麟搬运”店铺门前，将这一队伍身着斗篷的半人马团团围住。而他们似乎也没有反抗的迹象，就只是静静地站着不说话。
半人马的出现很快惊动了集市，整个港口码头都被疏散，麒麟军队领袖焦赭也很快赶到了现场。确认半人马们似乎没有敌意后，焦赭便走上前，开始与领头者交谈。
“虽然这不是第一次我们在港口见到半人马了，但你可能还是第一次，那我就解释一下。我们绝不可能让提雷克对这个港口感兴趣，所以半人马来到这里后选择只有三个：第一，在麒麟社群里住下永远不能回去。第二，我们将你迷晕，丢进丛林里自生自灭，不过放心，草药只会让目标失去记忆，并没有毒性。第三，最坏的情况，我们将迫不得已——”
领头者再次用拐杖敲了敲地，打断了焦赭的话。“看来你们并不认识我。那简单地说，就像你们在提防提雷克一样，提雷克也是我的敌人。我是来寻求合作的。”
焦赭显然没有预料到这个情况，此前的半人马，要么是无意间闯入的无知贵族，要么就是半人马殖民者，前者一般会得到前两个选项中的一个，而后者则一般得到第三个选项。正当焦赭张口想要详细询问时，领头者却抢先说道：“我不会回答你的问题。叫你们的领袖过来，这种大事我只能和最高领导者谈。”

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_9_o0]
额... 好吧？

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10]
可疑的合作

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10_desc]
翌日，僧达克刚刚踏进秋烨的树屋，秋烨立马开始了她的滔滔不绝：“僧达克，对吗？提雷克的老师，半人马的野心家，独角兽魔法的渴望者。看到你的背景，让我很难相信‘敌人的敌人是朋友’这句话。不过你的背景上倒也确实没有什么严重的罪行，额 —— 除了你曾经绑架过一只独角兽以外。总之，如果你不执着于所谓的‘合作’这件事，不如还是让我们给你和你们那些家伙安排一些好的住处。哦顺带一提，我们的音乐剧《歌剧魅影》最近在重映，当然，我是说，如果你们这群斗篷帮感兴趣搞搞公司团建的话。”
僧达克微微一笑：“真是个能说会道的领袖，我该如何称呼你？如果你真的做够了背景调查，你应该知道我是那种比较喜欢开门见山的半人马。我知道你们一直在防备着提雷克，不敢全面开放害怕吸引他的注意，所以如果我们一起除掉提雷克，你们获得彻底的自由，我获得我想要的魔力，这不是一场双赢吗？”
秋烨继续着长篇大论：“哦，哇哦！你想要干掉提雷克吗？我是说，我们不是没有想过，但是，你知道，提雷克可是个大家伙，我们可不想惹上他。你看着并不是多么强壮，哦抱歉，我是说你有点老，哦抱歉，我是说你看起来并不像是个能干掉提雷克的家伙。不过，如果你真的能帮我们解决提雷克，那我们当然会感激不尽！不过，你要知道，我们可不是那种轻易就会相信别人的 —— 哦对了，差点忘了，秋烨，你可以叫我秋烨。”
僧达克拿出一份书写潦草的文件：“我已经有方法了，不过如果在这里给你解释，恐怕我会听你把《歌剧魅影》整个剧本都叨叨完。自己看文件吧，拿定了主意就来联系我，我们的港口就在苹果嘉儿港对面的小岛上。” 说罢，僧达克转身离开了树屋。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_10_o0]
防止被剧透，聪明

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11]
僧达克的计划

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_desc]
在找到麒麟之前，僧达克和他的教团已经秘密联系了小马利亚各个地方的势力：提雷克的弟弟斯科潘、狮鹫、洛马基的科学家、甚至是无序与泽科拉。不过得到的结果却是非常失望的，如今如山一般的巨型提雷克，几乎是无敌的，不存在弱点。
如此一来，解决提雷克的方法只剩下了一个：蛮力。汇聚足够大量级的魔力，在一瞬间强行击穿提雷克的魔法护盾，将其击倒。僧达克的教团进行了严谨的计算，发现这一过程所需要的最小魔力量级，即使是一个天文数字，似乎并非不可能。
这大概需要汇聚一个国家量级的魔法，在小马利亚或者幻形灵帝国收集这样巨大量级的魔法，必然会引起当局的注意和处置，提雷克也会因此察觉。而唯一一个蕴含着大量魔力，却不被外界所知的地方，就是麒麟社群。

当然，要榨干麒麟全国的力量为一个成功性未知、回报也未知的疯狂计划服务，麒麟们自然不会同意这种离谱的合作。于是，僧达克提议通过三到五年的时间逐渐收集魔力，做为交换，他们将向我们传授黑魔法来弥补我们流失的魔力。而麒麟的贸易方面，他们也会补足全部的损失——只是，不要问钱从哪里来。

§R<=阅后即焚=>§!

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_o0]
同意合作

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_11_o1]
拒绝合作

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12]
走私案调查报告

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_desc]
当统计局对那五年的内部数据汇总分析时我们发现，消耗的稚马之息总量在其他地区均相对正常，略有超额，而唯独§2东部地区§!显著超额：仅占全国麒麟数量15%的东部地区竟然消耗了全国40%的稚马之息！
为什么这么明显的数据异常会被掩盖？为什么这么大的消耗量会被忽视？§2稚马之息在东部地区被有组织走私§!，这是我们的初步判断，而东部地区政府难逃其嫌。
专案组立刻派遣调查员前往东部地区，重点针对柔柔港以及海府等临近南部海岸的城市和村庄展开调查。但奇怪的是——我们§2没有在柔柔港§!找到任何一场花卉大量出口的记录、也没有发现任何走私码头和痕迹。
难道他们的犯罪组织是如此天衣无缝？还是调查组内也有内鬼？我们需要更多的线索，更多的证据。但至少，就目前我们所掌握的情报来看，以§2南都§!为中心，东部地区的各个省份都似乎牵扯其中。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_o0]
重点专案调查

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_12_TOOLTIP]
解锁系列决议：§Y走私专案§!

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13]
走私案调查报告

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13_desc]
当统计局对那五年的内部数据汇总分析时我们发现，消耗的稚马之息总量在其他地区均相对正常，略有超额，而唯独§2东部地区§!显著超额：仅占全国麒麟数量15%的东部地区竟然消耗了全国40%的稚马之息！
为什么这么明显的数据异常会被掩盖？为什么这么大的消耗量会被忽视？§2稚马之息在东部地区被有组织走私§!，这是我们的初步判断，而东部地区政府难逃其嫌。
专案组立刻派遣调查员前往东部地区，重点针对柔柔港以及海府等临近南部海岸的城市和村庄展开调查。但奇怪的是——我们§2没有在柔柔港§!找到任何一场花卉大量出口的记录、也没有发现任何走私码头和痕迹。
难道他们的犯罪组织是如此天衣无缝？还是调查组内也有内鬼？我们需要更多的线索，更多的证据。但至少，就目前我们所掌握的情报来看，以§2南都§!为中心，东部地区的各个省份都似乎牵扯其中。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13_o0]
不看了

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_13_o1]
下一页

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_14]
首都以及南部地区调查报告

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_14_desc]
经过调查，我们在§2首都以及南部地区§!发现了部分走私稚马之息的地方官员，已经严肃处理。然而，这些官员大多数都是独自行动、临时起意，而非有组织的走私团伙，多数也与东部地区的重大走私专案没有关联。
虽然这些独立案件与走私专案无关，但这些官员的走私行为都利用了一个相同的漏洞 —— 地方稚马之息因灾补缺申请表的审批流程过于宽松。这意味着，即使首都地区没有直接牵涉进走私专案，中央政府所制定的过于宽松的审批流程难辞其咎。
如今，这仅仅被解释为“流程设计上的失误”，但调查发现，在民众多次举报后，中央政府仅仅是要求地区政府严肃处理具体案件的官员，而并未对审批流程进行任何调整。§2中央政府内可能存在走私专案的包庇者§!，有意或者无意。

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_14_o0]
记录在案

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_15]
首都以及南部地区调查报告

[zh.EVENT_C18_MAIN_15_desc]
